- Revised 2026-11-07 09:05 at Will's direction with the DM context: contact is a woman who asked what grants he is pursuing and said she can definitely help; revision answers her question directly (no specific program chased — funding shape described so she can match it), uses his DM framing (day job, chicken-and-egg cold start on hardcore mode, 2130 kickstart purpose). File overwritten in place.
# phcc deficiency programme — methodical work-through plan

Coordinate: 19.5.9/7.5.8/6.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:30 CST
Request (verbatim): put together a plan to work through phcc deficiencies methodically
Status: Plan written 2026-11-07 22:31: ~/workspace/goals/finish-phcc/files/phcc-deficiency-plan.md — waves D1 (PQ-13, PQ-23) → D2 (versioned refs, _Float128) → D3 (PQ-22 GD-TLS) → D4 (VEX/EVEX) → D5 (bswap16/32, __auto_type) → D6 decision-gated studies (_Complex, C23) → D7 verification depth (conformance slice 2, arm64 gate, udivmoddi4 h7); phext refresh as a standing per-wave step; platform phases after the Linux queue. || D1 done 2026-11-07: F25 fixed, F26 partial (IFUNC residue -> D2), refresh landed; stack PUBLISHED at 8413d6f5 (main == exo). Next per plan: Wave D2. || D2 done 2026-11-07: F27 FIXED (static executables run — PQ-23 closed), F28 FIXED (versioned references + .symver), F29 PARTIAL (declaration half; TF128 codegen designed, not built), migrate BENCHMARKS fix in-tree, phext refresh landed; local stack on 8413d6f5, NOT pushed (publication is the parent's act). Will's priority ruling 2026-11-07 23:21, verbatim: "static builds are key, make sure we have support for that" — F27 was the wave's defining item; the wave report proposes a standing static gate cell set (static hello run, static Lua run, static phccbox smoke). Next per plan: Wave D3 (PQ-22 GD-TLS recon). || D2 PUBLISHED 2026-11-08: stack (37ac1bbe F27, f30d07bb F28, 73bf8d4a F29, 24660bed tooling, bdf12df2 refresh) pushed at bdf12df2 (main == exo, no force). Publisher verification from the stacked tree + fresh clone reproduced the wave: make test ALL PASSED, conformance 328/333 baseline five, PATCHES F1-F29 each once, refresh unpack 608/608 byte-identical. The standing static gate cells proposed by the wave were INAUGURATED and all passed: (1) static hello runs exit 0, 23 IRELATIVE in .rela.plt, bounds-symbols probe matches the section range exactly; (2) static Lua 5.4 fixed-script output byte-identical to dynamic; (3) static phccbox echo/wc/sed/grep/awk byte-identical to dynamic, awk prints 42. Next per plan: Wave D3 (PQ-22 GD-TLS recon). || D3 done 2026-11-08: F30 FIXED (PQ-22 closed — General-Dynamic/Local-Dynamic TLS: GOT pairs (DTPMOD64/DTPOFF64) in DLLs with the __tls_get_addr sequence live, GD→LE / GD→IE and LD→LE relaxation in executables, DTPOFF block-relative in DLLs, the static __tls_get_addr excuse; base measured first: wrong values in six GD/LD cells, linker segfaults in two (undefined GD symbols dereferenced sections[SHN_UNDEF]), one static link failure); F22's six IE cells + libmpfr witness unregressed; make test ALL PASSED; conformance 328/333 baseline five; standing static gate cells green; phext refresh landed (machine #3 note N21, gate STALE 0, unpack 608/608); local stack on bdf12df2 (df3941df F30 + efad39b2 refresh), NOT pushed (publication is the parent's act). Residues: relaxed executables keep a never-called __tls_get_addr PLT entry/dynsym import (cosmetic, pre-existing); TLSDESC (gnu2 dialect) still unhandled, fails loudly. Next per plan: Wave D4 (VEX/EVEX assembler frontier). || D3 PUBLISHED 2026-11-08: stack (df3941df F30 + efad39b2 refresh) pushed at efad39b2 (main == exo, no force). Publisher verification reproduced the wave on the stacked tree: clean build, make test ALL TESTS PASSED, conformance 328/333 baseline five (stamp HEAD@efad39b2), TLS spot cells rebuilt fresh (GD exe x defined, GD DSO x undefined) exact with rc 0, standing static gate cells green (hello 23 IRELATIVE + bounds probe matching the .rela.plt range exactly; Lua byte-identical; phccbox byte-identical, awk 42), PATCHES F1-F30 each exactly once, refresh phext dd878c07 unpack 608/608 byte-identical. Upstream sync #1 landed on top the same day (tip 5d36b9dd, base pin 70adbb12 — see 31.9.15/12.10.13/10.9.12). Next per plan: Wave D4 (VEX/EVEX assembler frontier). || D4 done 2026-11-08: F31 LANDED (assembler frontier closed — dedicated VEX/EVEX path beside the legacy machinery: asm_opcode_vex as an explicit prefix state machine (VSM_OPERANDS/CLASSIFY/PREFIX/OPCODE/MODRM/IMM/DONE), table-driven to the measured OpenSSL 4.1.0 perlasm surface (100 mnemonics, ~130,257 instruction lines; writemask/zeroing decorations only); BMI2 mulx + shifts + rorx + andn; supporting pieces: sal alias, jrcxz + forward R_X86_64_PC8, movbeq rows, legacy aesenc/aesenclast rows (upstream gap), {vex}/{evex} line prefixes (616 corpus lines). Perlasm census 12/42 -> 42/42 assemble; instruction streams semantically identical to GAS with ENCODING-DIFF 0 (standing F12 policy classes A-F counted: branch 5,057, pad 463, immform 186, shift1 168, disp 6, movabs 1; 58 aligner-unpaired fully dispositioned by identical key multisets / embedded-data decodes). OpenSSL Builds A (F17 recipe) and B (real AVX512 sources assembled in-build by phcc) both 2,183/2,183 objects, KAT exact (SHA-256 abc; AES-256-ECB FIPS vector). make test ALL PASSED; conformance 328/333 baseline five; D3 TLS spot cells green; standing static gate cells green on substance (two harness quirks named: D2 script's IRELATIVE counter reads 0 on readelf's truncated 'IRELATI V' type name — 23 entries present; static-phccbox cell invokes the multicall binary by the wrong argv[0] — binary correct, awk prints 42 as ./phccbox). Phext refresh landed (canonical e3c4d551, Design 364/364 CURRENT, verdict re-issued DIVERGENT-CLASSIFIED, unpack 610/610; stretch delivered: Design machine #5 — the prefix decoder in Slices 4-7 format — at 1.1.1/3.2.4/2.3.2 with register at Meta Sec 23; checker for #5 recorded as a gap, not a pass). Wave-boundary drift check: upstream mob tip == base pin 70adbb12 exactly, 0 commits past, no hot-file touches. Local stack on 5d36b9dd (6d854a95 F31 + 88806a61 refresh), NOT pushed (publication is the parent's act). Residues: loop-family forward branches not covered (jrcxz/jecxz only, the measured surface); unmeasured BMI2 (bextr/bzhi/pdep/pext/bls*) and broadcast forms fail loudly; {1toN}/{rn-sae} decorations rejected; static-hello symtab carries no __rela_iplt_* entries (nm: no symbols) — observation, F31 does not touch the synthesizing code. Next per plan: Wave D5 (bswap16/32 + __auto_type batch; F29 TF128 codegen is a candidate to join). || D4 PUBLISHED 2026-11-08: stack 6d854a95 (F31 VEX/EVEX + BMI2) + 88806a61 (phext refresh, canonical e3c4d551…) pushed, main == exo == 88806a61. Publisher verification on the stacked tree (clean rebuild per F31's header-dep lesson): make test ALL TESTS PASSED; conformance 328/333 baseline five, 0 splits; assembler spot (sweep3 semantic streams) — aes-cfb-avx512.s (EVEX) + rsaz-avx2.s (VEX-256) both POLICY-ONLY, ENCODING-DIFF 0, no unpaired keys; TLS spot cells GD exe defined + GD DSO undefined green (exact values, rc 0); standing static gate cells green measured directly (static hello runs, 23 IRELATIVE wide-readelf; bounds probe == .rela.plt range exactly on bounds-static, 22/22; static Lua byte-identical; static phccbox 5/5 smoke byte-identical, awk 42, invoked as phccbox); PATCHES F1–F31 each once + U1; unpack 610/610; machine #5 register present at Meta 1.1.1/1.2.10/1.23.1 (noted, not re-derived). Fresh clone: tip 88806a61, make test PASSED, static hello runs. Next per plan: Wave D5. || D5 done 2026-11-08 (TAKEOVER completion: the first D5 agent ended without a report at ~03:30 CST; F32/F33 were inherited as commits ded83817/7a7b6d3d on 88806a61 and re-verified by the takeover agent, F34 arrived as an uncommitted dirty tree): F32 FIXED (__builtin_bswap16/32/64, GNU semantics incl. unsigned-short return for the 16-bit form; corpora byte-identical to gcc+clang), F33 FIXED (__auto_type via two-pass initializer replay, follows gcc on the oracle splits; its three probe-corpus misses are the documented pre-existing _Generic-named-enum parser gap, proven identical on the pre-D5 base), F34 FIXED completing F29 (_Float128 value codegen on x86-64: TF128 helper dispatch, exact bignum literals, full conversion matrix; the inherited WIP carried four defects found by audit — float-ladder demotion computing F128 ops at 24-bit precision, inverted subnormal packing, dropped hex fraction digits, _Bool routed through double — all fixed in-commit and recorded in the F34 entry; corpora byte-identical to gcc, fuzz also to clang; static f128 runs). Stack: 2b740c85 (F34) + b8976f64 (phext refresh: canonical a91c24fb, 64,145 scrolls, seal 304df449, Design STALE 0, machines PASS/CURRENT with #3 note N22, verdict re-issued 63dad343 byte-reproducible, unpack 610/610), NOT pushed — publication is the parent's act. Regression net: make test ALL PASSED; conformance 330/333 with the exact probe mapping (b_gnu_009 + b_gnu_020 closed by F32/F33; set now [a_pp_018, b_gnu_015, b_gnu_016]); standing static cells green; D3 TLS spot cells green; D4 EVEX spot profile identical to the D4 control. Wave-boundary drift check: 0 upstream commits past 70adbb12 — no sync trigger. Named residue: phcc-compiled extern-__thread-to-DSO link gap (pre-existing on 88806a61, outside the D3 matrix) — future linker-wave candidate. Next per plan: Wave D6 (decision-gated studies: _Complex, C23 probe tier — no implementation until Will rules). || D5 PUBLISHED 2026-11-08: stack pushed at b8976f64 (main == exo, no force; ded83817 F32, 7a7b6d3d F33, 2b740c85 F34, b8976f64 refresh; base refs re-verified 88806a61 in the push exec). Publisher verification reproduced the wave from a clean rebuild of the stacked tree plus a fresh clone: make test ALL PASSED; conformance 330/333, diverge set exactly [a_pp_018, b_gnu_015, b_gnu_016], 0 oracle splits; PATCHES F1-F34 each once + U1; refresh phext a91c24fb unpack 610/610 byte-identical; F34 spots green (f128_basic byte-identical to gcc, f128_glob -static identical to dynamic — f128 also re-verified from the clone); TLS spot cells (GD exe defined, GD DSO undefined, genuine TLSGD objects) green; standing static gate cells green (hello 23 IRELATIVE by wide readelf; Lua byte-identical; static phccbox under the exact name phccbox byte-identical, awk=42). || D6 done 2026-11-08 (STUDIES ONLY, no compiler changes; rulings are Will's): _Complex study ~/workspace/goals/finish-phcc/files/phcc-complex-study.md — representation = struct-kind with interned Syms (BTYPE field is full: VT_F128 took the last slot, 15); layout parity measured on phcc itself; ABI needs exactly one special case (complex long double return via st0/st1 vs struct sret); Annex G comes free via the libgcc __mul*c3/__div*c3 calls both oracles emit; _Imaginary types rejected by BOTH oracles (non-item); _Float128 complex is oracle-split (gcc rejects, clang accepts) — priced out. Price: C1 declarations+components ~350-550 lines (unlocks rsa_complex.c + <complex.h> parse), C2 full arithmetic ~900-1300 lines. Recommendation: implement C1->C2. C23 study ~/workspace/goals/finish-phcc/files/phcc-c23-study.md + 34-probe tier at ~/workspace/phcc-conformance/c23/ (additive; baseline untouched): WORKS 7 / CLEAN-REJECT 12 / WRONG 5 / ORACLE-GAP 2 / ORACLE-SPLIT 8; WRONGs = C23 auto read as C89 implicit-int (garbage at runtime), int f(); accepted vs C23 f(void), #embed warn-and-delete -> empty array + garbage reads (x2), enum loose-form permissiveness. Oracles split on the newest surface: gcc 13 has no _BitInt on x86_64 and advertises 202000; clang 18 lacks constexpr but advertises 202311. Menu: L0 dialect plumbing (-std selector) + L1 additive surface ~550-900 lines (one wave, recommended), L2 +constexpr+#embed ~+550-950, L3 +_BitInt (width-capped) ~+1000-1800; 202311 honestly advertised only after L3, in c23 mode. Wave-boundary drift check: upstream mob HEAD still 70adbb12 — 0 commits past it, no sync trigger.

