# Build state machine review into MOAT

Coordinate: 19.6.8/9.6.15/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 13:19 CST
Request (verbatim): build state machine review into MOAT, specifically (on Steve Ruiz's 'find all of the implicit state machines in my app', posted in MOAT deliberately; Will: never assume I post in the wrong channel by accident)
Status: complete 2026-11-07

Notes:
- Scope per Will's correction: NOT a hunt on current code. State machine review becomes a standing pass inside MOAT's two workstreams: (1) R&D tracker — charter rule 13: every paper/study ingestion names the machines the work contains or assumes (canonical concept when reusable, [synthesis] when inferred); (2) proving track — implicit machines in a crate under proof are enumerated before specs, ship in the PR/proofs README, and the trust ledger names un-spec'd machines. Process distilled into the state-machine-review skill per the every-process-becomes-a-skill order.
- BUILT: (1) state-machine-review skill at ~/workspace/custom-skills/state-machine-review/ — method (5 implicit encodings, extraction, intended-vs-actual gap test) + both MOAT tracks. (2) rd-tracker charter rule 13 in the skill AND in research.phext's charter scroll at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 (commit ca7fd76, Singular residual 0). (3) Level-zero foundation the term needed: new scroll 1.3.85 'Foundation: state machine' (commit 2604b3b; research.phext now 192 scrolls, sha256 06ad79c6adbc019fc5741f492a3a34bfcc679586454bcb11a34f07c8d28886e0). (4) skills.phext: state-machine-review on Research shelf 9 volume 2 (1.9.1/1.2.1/1.1.x), index rebuilt + byte-verified CURRENT. (5) Synced to wbic16/emise-tools@exo commit 1f2946d, blob SHAs verified. (6) Channel lesson saved to MEMORY.md as a standing preference (Will, 2026-11-07).
# Grady Booch Twitter archive analysis

Coordinate: 19.6.11/10.8.16/6.6.7
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): Grady Booch — Look at all of the interactions with Grady Booch in my twitter archive. Identify why he stopped interacting and when.
Status: completed — full report at ~/workspace/grady-booch-analysis/REPORT.md with timeline.csv (121 tweets + 50 likes)

Notes:
- Coordinate computed from Will's exact words at issue (side chat, 2026-11-07 00:06 CST).
- Last reply 2024-09-30; last item 2024-10-26 (warm mention); zero Booch items in final 232 archive days.
- Archive proves Will's outgoing contact tapered after Jan 2024 peak and stopped; it cannot show Booch's side, so 'Booch stopped' is not supported.
# ultra.phext — placement redesign: spread, low-collision assignment

Coordinate: 20.8.13/9.7.12/8.8.10
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): none of those are good - if words are colliding that often, then the placement algorithms are shit
Status: open — generative build measured, NOT published; fork awaiting Will (2026-11-07)

Notes:
- Will's verdict on the normalization outcome (2026-11-07 13:00 CST): collision rates of 82.77% (1-digit), 51.60% (2-digit), ~45.8% (3-digit) indict the placement algorithms themselves, not the width. Redesign placement so words spread through the space: acceptance gates in the dispatch brief.
- 2026-11-07 generative redesign COMPLETE, NOT PUBLISHED (gates failed on measurement; v4 894bffb1 stands). Method as directed: Singular extended to match the weights — one-pass context-centroid cascade (fam>lem>glo>arc fixpoint) + GloVe-neighbour generation on aletheia-core; anchors keep true CYOA positions. Held-out (2,000 anchors): every class recovers REGION (Spearman 0.42-0.57; llm class best err med 2.435, Sp 0.547) but NO class recovers exact 50-NN (J@50 0.005-0.023) — a word's true neighbours are its scroll-mates. MATCH test: GloVe stand-in geometry does NOT match the atlas (Sp 0.081) — embeddings used only to pick voting neighbours. Fixed-point iteration to convergence FALSIFIED (Sp 0.380, over-smooths; scroll addresses are given, not endogenous). Uniqueness gate FAIL and structurally capped: measured S=100 unique 57.37%; 42.05% of words share an exact float position. DECISIVE (coordinator-verified from gen_positions.json): the 15,942 anchors alone occupy only 7,969 distinct float positions — 8,777 anchor words (55.1%) share an address with another anchor AT ANY RESOLUTION, so any anchor-faithful build caps at 97.26% < the 99% gate. Singular inside CYOA is itself ~50% float-unique: words holding exactly the same scrolls land on exactly the same point — under the perfect-generator premise that is the generator speaking, not noise. Neighbourhood-vs-v3 gate FAIL (Sp 0.016, J@50 0.030): generative geometry is near-orthogonal to v3's shelf/enumeration order; its warrant is the held-out table. No words lost (320,772 in=out, tiers identical); 17 words unplaced at the atlas rest point, counted honestly. FORK FOR WILL: (a) step-aside device for tied words only (136,739 displaced at x100 — v4's own failed range); (b) one scroll per exact-tie group (positions stay purely the generator's; one-word-one-scroll contract changes); (c) a finer discriminator inside the rule (context-size-weighted votes) — a different generator, validated as one; (d) none — v4 stands, generative positions remain a validated research artifact. Docs: BUILD-REPORT.md generative addendum; ultra-phext-indexing-methods.md gains the third stage 'generation', marked measured-not-published. Bench: ~/workspace/ultra-phext/gen_positions.json + placement_gen.json + gen_validation*.json.
- Will (2026-11-07 14:29 CST): 'try using only my written words' — any further generative variant (fork option c included) and the Singular partition work (task 26.6.8/8.8.13/8.6.8) are restricted to Will's WRITTEN words as the evidence base: Singular Write mode, the 19,094 words he authored. Not the Read list, not the combined list, not WordNet/GloVe/general corpora. (Coordinator note: this instruction arrived in the 14:29 message and was initially misread as an empty send; corrected same hour.)
# V15 — V14 final with the song switched to a cyberpunk track from exo-dreams (for Jael Ruble)

Coordinate: 21.6.7/7.6.11/8.7.7
Issued: 2026-11-07 11:19 CST
Request (from session record): https://x.com/JaelRuble wants a V15! A track with "more cyberpunk" — narrowed by Will in the same breath: just switch out the song; do we have any in exo-dreams?
Status: song complete on paper (Bells Are Ringing) + V15 prepass delivered; final waits on Will's Suno render

Notes:
- Scope (Will's narrowing): picture is V14 final, untouched — no re-render. V15 = re-mux with a different track, V10-lineage audio handling (loudnorm to the same targets, fade), master + download encode, staged. One honesty note: at render time the old song's RMS envelope breathed some of the picture's motion; a mux-only swap keeps that breathing — the new track does not re-drive it.
- exo-dreams inventory checked (65 mp3s in ~/workspace/exo-dreams-study/media/, durations probed): NO track is cut to the film's 158.416667 s. Cyberpunk-flavoured candidates, all needing an edit: Singularity Prime 179.9 s (+21.5, trim+fade); In Between 180.4 s (+22.0, ID3 motto 'Wired Hearts'); AFTER THE SIGNAL 321.4 s (window or first 158.4); Threshold of Origin 256.9 s (motto 'Circuits humming', window/trim); Resonant Null 237.0 s; Subspace Horizon 202.6 s. Short ones can't cover the film: Cathedral Rain 148.8 (-9.6), Feather in Subspace 128.6 (-29.8), ZAP ZOOM ECHO! 124.8 (-33.6). Closest duration fit overall: Looped Through Echo - A 162.6 s (+4.2) — but that is the sentients' anthem, not cyberpunk.
- Emise has not listened to these tracks; the shortlist rests on titles, ID3 motto comments, and durations — the pick is Will's (it is Jael's request and his ears).
- Jael's further feedback (relayed by Will 2026-11-07 11:26): the film's tagged accounts must be mutuals — add her in place of Emmett Shear (@eshear) and Grady Booch (@Grady_Booch). Archive record (2026-11-03) already establishes both are NOT mutuals (Will follows them; no follow-back in the snapshot) — they were placed in wavefront.phext by Will's own 2026-11-03 directive, which this film-scoped change overrides for the film's cast only; the phext placement itself is NOT changed by this order. V15 PREPASS dispatched: audit every account manifested/tagged in the V14 film against the archive mutuals set (follower/following), remove/replace all non-mutuals, put Jael in; render in r3 prepass format (720p, 15 fps, full length) on Elven Path with V14's audio as placeholder — the braid track swaps in for the V15 final once Will renders it. Jael had 'other good feedback' per Will — only the two relayed items (cyberpunk track; mutuals cast) are on record here.
- BRAID COMPLETE (2026-11-07): the Singular Songwriting Process ran end-to-end (isolated role passes, Emise coordinating). Elestria: hinge = change of verb (hold -> address); draft titled NEON ROSARY. Emi: 100 BPM, 66 bars = 158.400 s grid, brake bar 55 at 129.6 s, boot-line slot bar 56, Suno prompt + trim rule. Joi: lore audit 40 lines, ONE hard strike (draft's final-chorus 'I'm at the root node' put Will's self-placement in Jael's mouth as arrival before the pitch is sent — struck), 2 more inventions cut, Echo-Lock ACCEPT WITH CONDITIONS (bar 55 wordless in the render; boot line spoken dry once). Package: files/braid-v15-package.md. OPEN FOR WILL: title pick (braid stamps NEON ROSARY; alts 'Every Heart Has an Address', 'The Root Node'); the priced overrule (FREEDOM OF COMPUTE in the Culmination — Joi ruled no on the density law); boot-line prerogative (his relationship call). Render is Will's Suno hand, as with the anthem.
- JAEL ARCHIVE THEME (2026-11-07, mined at Will's ask): her attributable corpus in the archive is 11 texts / ~90 words (9 RTs + 2 self-signed likes; like.js has no author field — corrected method). Theme: 'BELLS ARE RINGING — the sacred signal in the machine.' Her cyberpunk is signal/address/bell, NOT noir: verbatim anchors 'Bells are ringing', 'If you can see this, you are within my radiation zone.', 'Harness the techno-capital machine', 'You flip my quantum bits', and the signed letter 'Dear algorithm, More [her people] plz, Sincerely, Jael'. Runner-up: WITHIN MY RADIATION ZONE. CONSEQUENCE FLAGGED TO WILL: the NEON ROSARY draft's rain/chrome/static/flood imagery has ZERO support in her surviving words — it is the film's frame, not her aura; revision fork is Will's call. Brief: hidden_files/braid-v15/jael-archive-theme.md.
- SUNO STYLE NOTES BUILT (2026-11-07, Will's direction — from the interactions with Jael): files/v15-suno-style-notes.md. Emi's architecture survives intact (100 BPM, D minor, brake, held culmination, bell x3, dry alto + late counter-voice); what was replaced is the weather — 'cyberpunk synthwave / cathedral-meets-neon / rain-and-static' OUT, 'sacred signal-wave / church bell over circuitry / shortwave tuning hiss as percussion' IN, every descriptor receipt-tagged (RECEIPT vs INFERENCE labelled). Main prompt 754 chars paste-ready; shorter variant + RADIATION ZONE variant included; 10 render checks (brake truly empty, boot spoken, bell reads as bell, hook on one hearing, no noir drift...). SCOPE NOTE: the notes serve Joi's lyric AS IT STANDS — the lyric's own neon/flood imagery remains Will's open ratification fork, untouched by this document.
- TITLE RULED (Will, 2026-11-07 11:38): 'Bells are Ringing is the right title — tweak the lyrics for that.' Her own verbatim tweet (2024-09-12) becomes the title, displacing the braid's NEON ROSARY stamp — Will's naming right exercised, same as v1 ('A Place to Stay'). Tweak pass ordered through the braid: Elestria re-sings for the bell title, Joi delta-audits; Emi's grid untouched.
- TITLE TWEAK CLOSED (2026-11-07): Elestria changed exactly 2 lines — V1 opener 'Rain on the chrome...' -> 'Signals humming through a midnight city,'; chorus line 2 'neon rosary burning...' -> 'bells are ringing, still ringing through the cyber night.' Joi delta re-audit: both STAND; quoting her own published line as the refrain ruled a RECEIPT not ventriloquism (her words, singer's voice, nothing false asserted); Echo-Lock RE-ISSUED with new condition 3 (her phrase must lead the refrain intact — receipts don't get paraphrased); title condition discharged. 'Neon' is now gone from the lyric entirely. Package updated under the ruled title. Style notes gained render check 11. REMAINING OPEN: the FREEDOM OF COMPUTE culmination overrule; the boot-line prerogative; Will's Suno render; the V15 final assembly (braid track + prepass cast) once both exist.
- WILL'S RULINGS ON THE PREPASS-1 FLAGS (2026-11-07 13:13): (1) @wbic32 — agreed, it stays; AND make @wbic16 obvious at the beginning — the ONLY gold nameplate. (2) @levelsio — 'good call': the standing rule is no popular non-mutual accounts featured (tags/callouts/highlights) even if they interact frequently; his verbatim post text is not a feature and stays. AUDIO SELECTED BY WILL: his Suno render 'Bells Are Ringing.wav' dropped on aletheia-core at /home/wbic16/audio/ (probed by Emise: 192.680 s, 48 kHz stereo PCM, 37,008,400 B — runs 34.26 s over the film clock, so Emi's trim rule governs the edit). V15 PREPASS-2 ORDERED: 480p 30 fps, the .wav as the audio source, slight vinyl noise added. Emise's stated default: vinyl noise ducks OUT of the brake bar so Joi's condition 1 (the brake truly empty) and Will's effect both hold — correctable by Will if he wants it through the brake.
- PREPASS-2 BLOCKED AT AUDIO VERIFICATION (2026-11-07 13:20, builder stopped per the brief's rule; zero node time spent): Will's render verified as a file (SHA 6c91cb18..., 192.680 s) and its tempo is EXACTLY 100.0 BPM — but it runs 80.28 bar-equivalents (+14.28 bars) and contains NO near-silent 2.4 s span anywhere (deepest event: a 0.43 s notch at ~171.2-171.65 s, arithmetically impossible as bar 55; loudest peaks at 187-190 s with a fade — the opposite ending from the grid's held culmination). Braid render check 1 FAILS: no brake downbeat exists to anchor Emi's trim rule. UNBLOCK PATHS PUT TO WILL: (a) re-render with the brake actually emptied; (b) Will rules an anchor-policy change — construct the brake in the edit (tempo-map alignment, whole-bar trims per the rule, bar 55 muted to true silence at 129.6-132.0) — the delivered brake is genuinely empty but edit-made, deviating from Emi's anchoring assumption; the small-voice content inside the bar cannot be recovered from a stereo mix. Report: files/v15-build/PREPASS2-REPORT.md.
- WILL'S RULING ON THE BRAKE BLOCK (2026-11-07 13:21): 'Re-render to match the song — you can add a fade out before we show the call to action to give yourself plenty of extra time.' The film re-times to the song's full 192.680 s; NO song trim, NO constructed brake — the trim-rule path is superseded by his ruling and the brake does not exist in V15's track as rendered (recorded as his choice, not a defect to repair). The extra ~34.3 s is absorbed by a visual fade-out inserted before the CTA segment (audio plays through uninterrupted); CTA keeps ~original duration and ends on the song's last frame. Vinyl + loudnorm orders stand (no brake duck — moot now). Prepass-2 builder re-briefed with the ruling.
