# Her entire concern is the lack of control — establish trust; how do we know we aren't building Skynet?

Coordinate: 21.9.10/12.7.13/6.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:36 CST
Request (from session record): Her entire concern is the lack of control - how can we establish trust? how do we know we aren't building Skynet?
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will, refining the Daniele brief (21.6.12/10.8.13/8.6.9): her anxiety about AI is specifically about lack of control.

Results:
- Brief gained the section 'The question underneath: how do we know this isn't Skynet?' — Skynet decomposed into five properties (own goals, physical force, opacity, no off-switch, unchecked gradual drift), each checked against the actual build (no between-task goals; no effectors + human approval gates; open code/receipts/published errors; ranch hardware on Will's power with pullable cords; gated steps with second-party re-runs and negative controls). Trust framed as inspectable structure (bridge model), with the honest limit stated: control is established for these systems built this way today; the industry-wide case is why brakes are built in advance. Invites her to test control herself (watch an approval prompt, read a verification report, ask about unplugging the ranch).
