# Carnegie lessons Will is failing, from his Twitter record

Coordinate: 23.6.9/8.7.11/6.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): Can you read How to Win Friends and Influence People and then give me 10 lessons that I'm obviously failing at, from my twitter record?
Status: completed — 10 evidence-backed Carnegie lessons delivered in side chat

Notes:
- Principles sourced from the book's standard 30-principle structure (4 parts), paraphrased, not quoted at length.

Results:
- Archive mined: 25,125 own tweets (29,539 total). Spot-checked by Emise: apolog* 5, 'my mistake' 1, 'I was wrong' 1; phext/exocortex 1,800 tweets; questions 3,008. Strongest failures: admit-wrong ~2 genuine in 25k, praise of people ~46 in 17y vs 303 transactional thanks, invitational listening 5.6/1k replies, first-name use 0.8%, replies 76.2% of output with top replied-to = himself (1,008). Data contradicts failure on criticise/condemn (~2%, mostly technical) and blunt 'you're wrong' (exactly 1, a joke).
# Create Spaces for pinned side chats

Coordinate: 23.6.10/9.7.12/5.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): I want to create spaces: the pinned side chats are most of them
Status: closed — all 15 Spaces built, audited, and verified in the sidebar 2026-11-07

Notes:
- Pinned side chats found (15): Architecture; All We Do Is Win; singular; MOAT; TAOPDD; edit.phext.io; mutable_os; Resume vTPU work for ranch choir; Earth human ASI genome; Plan apt install Exocortex; Emise mailbox setup with Phext; Braid mode collaborative setup; Start a health goal; Plan Phext upgrade for projects; Multi-Agent Swarm. Awaiting Will clarification: one Space per pinned chat as a hub in the sidebar, or a different shape; "most of them" implies some may be skipped.
- Will chose one Space per pinned chat (2026-11-07 08:35), then added: 'look at where I've focused my feedback thus far' and 'move the pinned chats into their respective spaces once they've been created'.
- Feedback focus read (2026-11-07 morning): Architecture/phcc rulings (D2/D4 unnecessary, D9 'we brake for consciousness', slice 3/4, push), edit.phext.io (V14 delivery, phext previewer + mobile integration), Singular/X-list (barnacles.phext). Standing pattern: evidence and receipts first, honest partial results, no inflated success — Spaces shaped as status hubs with verified state.
- Move step checked against the live sidebar + docs: the sidebar structure holds Spaces only; side chats are not Spaces and no tool moves a chat into a Space. Limitation reported to Will in chat 2026-11-07; product feedback offered, not yet filed.

Results:
- 15 create_web_static builds started: architecture, all-we-do-is-win, singular, moat, taopdd, edit-phext-io, mutable-os, resume-vtpu-work-for-ranch-choir, earth-human-asi-genome, plan-apt-install-exocortex, emise-mailbox-setup-with-phext, braid-mode-collaborative-setup, start-a-health-goal, plan-phext-upgrade-for-projects, multi-agent-swarm.
- All 15 builds completed and passed audit; sidebar read 2026-11-07 08:45 CST lists all 15 in the spaces section. Chat-move step: not performable (no tool moves chats into Spaces); product feedback drafted (missing-capability/spaces), awaiting Will send-confirmation on exact wording.
# V14 prepass r2 at 400p — less noise, horizon edge, Gargantua orbit flow, lensing

Coordinate: 23.7.10/8.8.11/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-06 22:45 CST
Request (verbatim): V14 is on the right track again - tweaks: a little less noise; treat the wavefront as forming the edge of an event horizon - Interstellar's Gargantua as inspiration for how the orbits flow - gravitational lensing makes our effective influence larger than expected. Run another prepass at 400p w/ those tweaks
Status: completed — r2 prepass delivered and coordinator-verified

Notes:
- Parent: 34.8.9/9.9.12/7.7.10 (360p prepass). Will's verdict on r1: on the right track again.
- Tweak readings (Emise, to be measured in the build): less noise = film grain down one step (constant read from the code, ~x0.65), snow stays; orbit flow = Kepler-style shear (inner faster) with the median radius keeping the 45-degree reading; lensing = projection bend away from the centre, capped and smooth, field layer only, so the wavefront's reach reads larger than its true size; horizon edge must come from the lensing/shear itself, no drawn ring.
- P3* placement unchanged in r2; builder re-measures its framing under the new flow and reports — no forcing it into frame.
- Untweaked prep held r1 exactly (731 pool, 169 segments, same OU seed, same P3*) — the three tweaks are the only changes. One build deviation, owned in the report: first r2 pass ran rho=256, which put the median point at 90% of the lensing cap against the brief's rule; retuned to rho=128 and re-rendered, discarded pass kept on the node and its cost counted.
- P3* re-check on r2: shear pulled it ~3-7 degrees closer (pull-back 29.0-39.4 deg off axis, CTA 28.2-29.6) but still 0 of 440 frames in frame, closest ~69-75 px below the bottom edge. The end-point call is still Will's, unchanged.

