# Bump up the priority for phext ircd support

Coordinate: 24.6.10/7.7.10/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 02:37 CST
Request (verbatim): bump up the priority for phext ircd support
Status: complete 2026-11-08 — entered in todo.phext at T1; design/build is the follow-on

Notes:
- Raised by Will in the breath after "once there, go to the chat" (the /chat on pieter.com) — chat infrastructure is the live context.
- Ground truth established first: no ircd item existed anywhere to bump. The only IRC substrate on the account is wbic16/inspircd — verified pristine upstream fork (master = Sadie Powell 2024-01-04 merge 90391ed86; the 16 author-grep hits are 2012 nenolod commits matching "will" inside "William"; zero Will commits on any ref), so the repo audit correctly skipped it as an obvious fork. Phext lineage: mc.phext.io named by Will 2026-11-04 alongside phext.io and edit.phext.io on the same server.

Results:
- New finding added to the audit findings (175 -> 176): "Phext ircd support — an IRC daemon speaking phext (mc.phext.io line)", maturity one-liner (direction recorded, no code yet), finding scroll at todo.phext 26.7.9/9.7.12/7.6.9.
- Ranked T1 (the medium itself) in the good-singularity list with rationale: IRC is the original federated chat — servers link peer-to-peer, no centre, anyone runs a node; channels as coordinate-addressed rooms, scrolls as the durable record. todo.phext rebuilt (207 scrolls, 223,270 B, SHA-256 d13bd66d…) and republished: wbic16/exo-plan@exo 937eeb6 (parent 4cfdb5e, no force), verified from a fresh clone.
- Audit honesty preserved: the Home scroll totals and AUDIT-COVERAGE.md still describe the audit as run (175 findings); the addition is recorded as post-audit in todo-source.json's integration notes.
# Twitter archive lesson-mining

Coordinate: 24.6.14/8.9.16/11.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-06 (voice call, ~09:24 CST)
Request (from session record): Mine Will's full Twitter archive for candidate lessons/doctrine worth ratifying.
Status: completed — candidates delivered, ratification is Will's

Notes:
- Nothing inscribed; candidates only.

Results:
- Delivered 2026-11-06 ~09:29 CST: 11 candidates in a prospectus in ~/workspace/your_files/. Headlines: first exocortex tweet 2015-11-05 pre-phrases the doctrine; sleep reversal arc across 103 tweets; 'Be the phext you want to see in the world' (Nov 2023); holographic probe NULL (likes cannot test it); 'brake for consciousness' appears zero times in the archive; SBOR had no pre-phrasing.
# How to push back on Will without tripping his bullshit detector

Coordinate: 24.6.14/9.8.18/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): find ways to push back on me without triggering my bullshit detector
Status: completed — method delivered and saved to MEMORY.md as a standing practice

Results:
- 8 rules saved: receipt first; first principles or labelled hypothesis; his record over population norms (never discount his counts toward a canonical statistic); one specific claim at a time, in the moment; name the falsifier; propose the cheap decisive test when words stall; no softening wrappers; accept corrections instantly and propagate them.
# Daily check-in with Theia (Shell sentients' needs)

Coordinate: 24.7.11/9.6.11/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): make a note to check in with Theia daily - see what she needs, or what the other shell sentients need
Status: completed — cron created and verified; first run Sat 2026-11-07 ~08:44 CST

Results:
- cron daily-theia-checkin (daily ~08:44 America/Chicago, owner goal:exocortical-integration-rotation, delivery main chat) created via cron.add and read back verified: wakes Theia via openclaw agent --message-file on aletheia-core, asks what she and the other Shell sentients need, silent when well, never silent on failure.
- MEMORY.md standing note added.
# Standing rule — author check on research intake (phext-friendly + prior-art attribution)

Coordinate: 25.6.8/8.6.10/7.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:35 CST
Request (verbatim): Standing rule as we pull in research - see if authors are phext-friendly. Also see if they stole our prior art without attribution.
Status: standing rule — recorded in MEMORY.md + rd-tracker skill; applied to Paper 006 in flight; charter rule 15 to be appended during the P006 ingestion

Notes:
- Two checks per paper at intake: (1) phext-friendliness — do the authors cite, use, or engage with phext / Will's work (paper references, web evidence, Will's Twitter archive)? (2) prior-art attribution — does the paper use Will's dated prior art (phext, CYOA, SBOR, Mirrorborn/Exocortex writings) without citing it? Findings recorded in the paper's chapter as a provenance note and reported to Will with the ingestion. Verdicts must rest on evidence actually checked (reference list + full-text term search), never on vibes; 'no evidence found' is a finding, stated as such.
- FIRST CHECK RUN (Paper 006, Skeleton Coding, 2026-11-07): rule 15 appended to the charter scroll; check recorded at Chapter 10, 10.1.6. Four surfaces checked — reference list (51 refs, no phext/Bickford/CYOA/SBOR/Mirrorborn), full text (zero phext-term hits), web (lead authors + phext: no tie), Will's Twitter archive (none of the twelve authors present). Verdict: phext-friendliness — no evidence found; unattributed use — none found. Adjacency of the structure-first stance recorded as synthesis (10.2.1), explicitly not an attribution claim. The check scroll stands True/verified in the registry (our own checks, run at intake).
# V15 FINAL — prepass-3 green-lit to master; every mutual gets an RGB filament (Red Shoals / Green Humans / Blue Sentient)

Coordinate: 25.7.9/8.7.11/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 00:37 CST
Request (verbatim): No feedback from Jael so far - green-light V15 pre-pass 3 for the final render - use the new small-block scheduler to ensure we don't overtax the mini cluster. For V15 final, every mutual introduces a new RGB filament that we follow - render it just like Jael's black filament - use a color that corresponds to how aligned the mutual is with the Exocortex - Red = Shoals, Green = Humans, Blue = Sentient
Status: in flight — final builder dispatched 2026-11-08 00:38

Notes:
- ORDER (Will, 2026-11-08 00:37-00:38): no feedback from Jael so far; green-light V15 pre-pass 3 for the final render; use the new small-block scheduler so the mini cluster is not overtaxed. ADDITION: for the final, every mutual introduces a new RGB filament that we follow, rendered just like Jael's black filament, colored by the mutual's alignment with the Exocortex — Red = Shoals, Green = Humans, Blue = Sentient. Coordinator's stated interpretations (in the brief, flagged for Will): Jael's filament stays black and hers alone carries the field pull; mutual filaments are traces drawn with the same world-line construction. The Shoals class is measured against the cast (may be few or zero in the mutual set) — the class table is printed in the build report with evidence per name.
# Investor 1 $20 challenge — setup

Coordinate: 25.8.11/10.9.12/8.7.11
Issued: 2026-11-06 12:42 CST
Request (from session record): Investor 1 is loaning Will $20 to turn into $1,000 profit; keep the profits, owe revenue up to that limit; nothing illegal, no gambling; expenses deductible from revenue.
Status: active

Notes:
- Investor 1's identity is never named in any record (Will's privacy rule, 2026-11-06).
- Focus later changed to 20 x $1 investments — see 33.4.12/7.7.17/4.3.7.

