# Doomer Support System — Slop Blocker products

Coordinate: 26.5.7/7.5.9/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-07 19:34 CST
Request (verbatim): Doomer Support System

Slop Blocker products
- help people opt out of the AI content tsunami if they don't want to deal with it 
- provably human content
- slop fighter
Status: v1 built — phext-lattice integration (branch + links) and merge/deploy are Will's steps

Notes:
- Idea drop in side chat 2026-11-07; no prior Doomer Support System product in memory (Doomer.phext is a separate register of safety-motivated opponents).
- Landscape checked 2026-11-07: 'Slop Blocker' name taken repeatedly (slopblocker.app, SlopBlocker.ai, Munene AI Slop Blocker $4.99 lifetime / 350+ users); blockers mostly free; detection is an arms race and cannot carry 'provably'; declaration badges (Not By AI, Authors Guild $10/title) are honor-system; C2PA provenance is checkable but proves signer declaration, not humanness.
- Recommended entry: Support System pack first (done-for-you opt-out using existing tools + maintained lists), Provably Human seal built inside edit.phext.io (counted typed/pasted/machine shares, signed, phext scroll), Slop Fighter reports feed the shared list. Blocker-first entry ruled out.
- DECISION (Will, 2026-11-07 19:52 CST, via options tap): build first as a free public utility, revenue second. Paid Support System pack parked. Form follows Will's 2026-11-01 public-utility rule: self-contained, no login, no backend, linked from main UI.
- v1 scope: kit generator from vetted existing tools + downloadable blocklist file + pre-2022-11-30 search + Slop Fighter report builder (copy-out, no backend). No detector in v1. Provably Human seal is phase 2 inside edit.phext.io; v1 carries only the explainer and exact claim wording.
- Follow-on task (Will, 2026-11-07 20:12 CST): 'differentiate what we can offer from the crowd' — its own reference coordinate computed at issue; differentiation work rides on this parent scroll per the session thread.
- Differentiation pass completed 2026-11-07 (task 16.7.9/8.6.11/7.6.13): matrix in brief; page updated (27,139 B, sha dcf2e4ac...).
- RULING (Will, 2026-11-07 21:04 CST, task 28.6.8/7.6.10/8.5.9): 'we don't block people or bots, or content — we block misalignment.' Origin (human/bot, AI/handmade) is not the criterion; mismatch is: claims vs reality (undisclosed AI presenting as human), maker's game vs viewer's intent (algorithm farming), platform's serve vs user's stated opt-out. Brief, page, and MEMORY corrected in the same session.
- Misalignment ruling propagated 2026-11-07 evening: brief + page (30,006 B, sha d9cecbfc...) + README + MEMORY all carry it; origin-framing superseded wherever it conflicted.
- NAMING CORRECTION (Will, 2026-11-07 21:33 CST, task 18.7.11/9.6.10/6.6.9): 'Doomer Support System' cannot be said to someone who cares about human flourishing and Skynet. Name retired for the public system; rename candidates presented, pick is Will's. Product work (utility, brief) stands under whatever name he chooses.
- NAME SETTLED (Will, 2026-11-07 21:34 CST): the system is the Alignment Support System. Public strings renamed across page/brief/README/MEMORY; legacy internal paths unchanged.

Results:
- Brief: ~/workspace/your_files/doomer-support-system-brief.md — three products (Blocker / Seal / Fighter), three priced entries, kill gates, one open decision (paid pack first vs free public utility first).
- v1 utility built 2026-11-07: ~/workspace/doomer-support-system/slop-blocker.html (25,282 B, SHA-256 1ef10f14...) — self-contained, no login/backend/api, JS syntax-checked, all JS-referenced ids present, zero external assets. Kit generator (vetted tools only, real prices/limits), pre-2022-11-30 + links-only search, Slop Fighter list downloads (uBlacklist/uBlock/hosts, client-side) + report formatter, Provably Human explainer (seal = phase 2, no badge shipped). README carries the edit.phext.io integration steps and the HUGE-list freshness note (fork reports original ceased Nov 2025).
- Post-rename page: ~/workspace/doomer-support-system/slop-blocker.html — all public strings carry 'Alignment Support System', zero 'Doomer' mentions in the page.
