# Patch programme: phcc builds the benchmark project matrix (publication gate)

Coordinate: 27.6.10/8.6.13/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): before we publish phcc as a real competitor, we need to patch it to build those projects, too
Status: Patch programme COMPLETE (F1-F24, gate GREEN at d0659ba4); deficiency waves D1 (F25/F26) PUBLISHED at 8413d6f5, D2 (F27/F28/F29) PUBLISHED at bdf12df2, D3 (F30, PQ-22 closed) PUBLISHED at efad39b2; upstream sync #1 landed on top (tip 5d36b9dd, base pin 70adbb12). Open queue per the deficiency plan: D4 (VEX/EVEX), D5 (bswap16/32, __auto_type; F29 TF128 codegen a candidate), D6 studies (_Complex, C23), D7 (conformance slice 2, arm64 gate, udivmoddi4 h7). Standing per-wave steps now include the phext refresh, the three static gate cells, and the wave-boundary upstream drift check.

Results:
- F8 d5d1f2f6: float.h C11 completion; sed gnulib 222/287 pass 0 fail, grep gnulib 257/315 pass 0 fail; probe identical across 3 compilers.
- PQ-4 FIXED (F7, local commit 10ef1f5b on 229ad47c, ~/workspace/phcc-pq4/tree, not pushed): C11 char16_t/char32_t literals (u/U prefixes) implemented by extending the L-literal machinery - encoding-parametrized parser in tccpp.c, types + generalized string initializers in tccgen.c, four token kinds + widened TOK_HAS_VALUE in tcc.h, new include/uchar.h, win32 uchar.h gate widened. Differential probes byte-identical under gcc 13.3.0 / clang 18.1.3 / phcc (incl. surrogate pairs, mixed concatenation, macro-carried literals, #if, _Generic); oracle split on out-of-range char16 constants follows gcc. FFmpeg reproducer passes; FFmpeg builds past shared.c through ~1,600 objects, then stops at FOUR new isolated blockers (reproducers in ~/workspace/phcc-pq4/repro-next/, numbers for parent to assign): (a) mathops.h 'i'-constraint/__builtin_constant_p idiom ~190 TUs, (b) SSE register clobbers rejected (%xmm0), (c) SSE/MMX opcodes missing from tcc asm (movdqa/pshufd/xorps/...), (d) designated initializer on anonymous-aggregate member (libswscale/format.c:977). Plus one non-compiler failure: sys/sysctl.h configure-detection divergence (libavutil/cpu.c). phcc make test ALL PASSED; conformance spot re-run unchanged 328/333. Phext STALE on refresh: Source scrolls tccpp.c/tccgen.c/tcc.h/win32-include-uchar.h + new include/uchar.h unplaced; bindings machines #1, #2, #4; Design views for those files; gate verdict. Machine #3, libtcc1 receipts, assembly listings untouched.
- PQ-3 FIXED (F10, local commit 9761eaa3 on 229ad47c, branch pq3-version-script, ~/workspace/phcc-pq3/tree + phcc-pq3.bundle, not pushed): --version-script implemented with GNU ld semantics in tccelf.c (+813/-13), libtcc.c (+6), tcc.h (+9); PATCHES.md F10. Grammar: named + anonymous nodes, global:/local: lists, literals + globs (* ? [...] POSIX classes), quoted names, extern blocks, one dependency per node, merged multiple scripts; hard errors (GNU wordings, no output file) for syntax, duplicate global/local expression, anonymous combined with named, undefined dependency, unreadable file, and non-link outputs. Matching precedence established empirically vs GNU ld (exact-global first node, exact-local beats wildcard-global, wildcard-global last node, wildcard-local, else plain). Application composes with machine #3: set_elf_sym branch order untouched; demote pass after resolve_common_syms; verdicts recorded at export_global_syms/bind_libs_dynsyms; ABS version symbols before create_gnu_hash; VERDEF byte-identical layout (BASE entry, empty nodes kept, dependency verdaux, SysV hash); shared versym index space with VERNEED allocated after definitions; empty-verneed emission bug found by consumer test and fixed (guard counts from post-definition baseline). Evidence: 15-case probe corpus byte-compared vs GNU ld (dynsym + VERDEF + DT tags) all match; consumer interop under gcc-built and phcc-built consumers (dlvsym present/absent correct, localized symbol not dlsym-able). OpenSSL 4.1.0 verbatim no-asm/no-shared recipe: legacy.so now links with providers/legacy.ld exporting exactly OSSL_provider_init (gcc's exports the same one symbol); build then stops at apps/openssl unresolved libcrypto refs - reproduced identically with pre-F10 F6 baseline, a separate pre-existing archive-resolution limitation (new PQ candidate, wave 3). Shared no-asm build completes fully: libcrypto.so.4 VERDEF byte-identical to gcc build, 5693 OPENSSL-versioned exports in both, 0 leaks past libcrypto.ld, built apps/openssl runs (SHA-256 verified). make test ALL PASSED; conformance spot re-run unchanged 328/333 (same five documented (b) divergences). Two implementation bugs found and fixed en route: uninitialized lexer failed flag (parse silently no-op at -O2) and dynarray_reset double-free (it frees elements itself). STALE on next phext refresh: machine #3 binding + its machine description (resolution order unchanged; demote pass + export-point recording to be added), tccelf.c Design view, gate verdict; tcc.h/libtcc.c Source scrolls.
- F12 assembler completion cluster COMPLETE (local commit 6f116f70 on 229ad47c, ~/workspace/phcc-asm/tree, NOT pushed; PATCHES.md F12 with lettered parts a-g): (a) .section full GAS option grammar (flags/@type/entsize/group-shape), GAS-verified; two deliberate divergences recorded - option-less sections keep TCC's SHF_ALLOC default (tcctest .data.ignore is load-bearing evidence; GAS gives novel sections no flags) and the perlasm #alloc premise is corrected (on x86-64 ELF GAS treats # as comment: the note section gets NO SHF_ALLOC, readelf-verified). (b) same-section asm-label differences in data directives deferred and patched at unit end (perlasm .long 1f-0f idiom, 126 occ.); cross-section/. cases keep the PC-relative reloc path. (c) .comm with GAS merge semantics in both -fcommon (SHN_COMMON) and -fno-common (.bss) modes, symbol-table-verified vs GAS. (d) base-less SIB operands (,reg,scale) byte-identical vs GAS. (e) %xmm8-%xmm15 registered (tokens outside the contiguous register block; encoder unchanged); ymm/zmm deliberately absent (no VEX/EVEX). (f) opcode coverage: movdqa/movdqu/movapd/movupd/movsd/movhlps/andps(+i386)/andnps/orps/xorps/shufps/paddq/pshufd/pshuflw/pshufhw/pshufw/pinsrw/pslldq grp7/psrldq grp3/movntq/movntdq/punpcklqdq/punpckhqdq, packed-double family, SSSE3 0F38 family via new OPC_0F38 (pmulhrsw byte 0x0B per GAS), adcx/adox, movbe, pushfl/popfl aliases; pavgb/pavgw widened to MMX forms; two baseline defects fixed (movaps/movups register-source mask; SSSE3 double-66). All forms byte-compared vs GAS incl. a 24-instruction census probe (90 bytes, MATCH) and i386 cross-build probes vs GAS --32. (g) PQ-7: inline-asm xmm0-15 clobbers accepted and recorded in clobber_regs (NB_ASM_REGS grown; slots permanently marked allocated in constraint solving; %-prefix stripped for all register clobbers - %rax also failed at baseline; mm0-7 accepted no-ops like cc/flags); clobber-list parser now concatenates adjacent string literals (FFmpeg "%"FF_REG_a idiom). Acceptance: OpenSSL perlasm 12/42 assemble fully (CFI-stripped copies; unstripped files all stop first at .cfi = sibling F9); the 12 differ from GAS only in four pre-existing TCC policy classes (jump relaxation, NOP fill, shift-by-one form, branch addend-in-RELA), each reproduced with the pristine baseline assembler. Remaining 30 classified: 5 BMI2 mulxq, 4 VEX-128-only, 21 VEX-256/EVEX; vzeroupper/vzeroall special-casing measured and rejected (294-5881 further VEX lines per file, zero files completed). FFmpeg 9.0.2 full build: every assembler-blocked TU compiles (configure now reports HAVE_XMM_CLOBBERS 1); remaining failures exactly 223x PQ-6 mathops 'i'-constraint, sysctl configure item, PQ-11 excess initializers, shared.c (F7 territory). make test ALL PASSED; conformance spot re-run unchanged 328/333, diverge set [a_pp_018, b_gnu_009, b_gnu_015, b_gnu_016, b_gnu_020], oracle split 0. STALE bindings: Source scrolls + Vol 3 segmentations + Design views + gate verdict for tccasm.c, tcctok.h, tcc.h, i386-asm.c, i386-tok.h, i386-asm.h, x86_64-asm.h, i386-gen.c, x86_64-gen.c; no section-A.3 machine file edited; libtcc1 proof receipts untouched.
- PQ-12 FIXED (F16, local commit e0b58d42 on 229ad47c, branch pq12-common-extraction, ~/workspace/phcc-pq12/tree, not pushed): archive extraction follows GNU ld's rule, measured first over a 17-cell probe matrix (~/workspace/phcc-pq12/probes/). Standing UNDEF pulls for strong/weak/common member defs; weak UNDEF never pulls; standing COMMON pulls only for a STRONG member def; decision at archive-encounter order. Fix is two hunks in tccelf.c (+78/-2): (1) tcc_load_alacarte criterion UNDEF-and-not-weak or COMMON, the COMMON case gated by new member_def_is_strong() peeking at the member's own symtab; (2) set_elf_sym: the brief's premise that the branch order already displaces a common was verified FALSE for bss definitions (IS_BSS lumps SHN_COMMON with SHT_NOBITS - a pulled member's .bss def lost to the standing common and the rescan re-pulled it, erroring 'defined twice'), fixed by one branch: SHN_COMMON patched by any real-section definition. All 17 probe cells match ld (R5 0->42; 4+32 commons displaced by size-16 def; size-64 bss def displaces size-4 common; C6 side-effect errors like ld; --whole-archive 42 both). make test ALL PASSED gcc-built and self-hosted (gcc-linked self-host suite fails identically on base = PQ-1 signature). Conformance spot re-run unchanged 328/333, same five (b) divergences. git 2.56.0 builds + smoke; zlib --static test OK (shared = PQ-1, base-present); OpenSSL no-shared failure signature byte-identical to base (128 unresolved, same set - F10/F14 territory). Left alone deliberately: common x common merge keeps first size (4 vs ld 32) = machine #3 note N6's documented divergence; C4b two strong defs (bss+data, no archive) silent under phcc - pre-existing, unchanged. PATCHES.md F16 carries the PROPOSED replacement text for machine #3's ABSENT sentence, note N7 and an I10 clause (phext not edited). STALE on refresh: machine #3 binding + description, tccelf.c Design view, gate verdict, tccelf.c Source scroll. Report ~/workspace/phcc-pq12/REPORT.md.
- PQ-11 FIXED (F15, local commit 06263c94 on 229ad47c, ~/workspace/phcc-pq11/tree, NOT pushed): excess initializers warn-and-discard instead of hard error 'too many initializers' — new DIF_DISCARD flag + decl_excess() in tccgen.c (+94/-10). Oracle boundary mapped empirically first (gcc 13.3.0/clang 18.1.3, 44 probes): warn+discard for positional excess (array/struct/union/scalar braces/compound literals/nested per-container); discarded elements fully parsed but NEVER evaluated (side-effect counters stay 0 — the 'gcc evaluates them' belief is false), no conversion/constant checks; still errors: designated OOB, range overrun, unknown field; flex-member growth warns in neither oracle nor here. gcc followed on both splits: brace group as excess of exhausted struct/union = hard error 'extra brace group'; designators inside discarded groups validated. 44/44 probes pass (rc/error/warning-presence/values identical to oracle consensus). make test ALL PASSED after ONE justified expectation update: tests2 60_errors_and_warnings test_conflicting_array_definition expected the old error; both oracles emit the new warning text verbatim — expect updated in-commit. tcctest has no initializer-error expectation. Conformance spot re-run UNCHANGED 328/333, diverge set exactly the baseline five (no probe covered excess initializers — no classification moved). FFmpeg: the motivating sighting libswscale/format.c:977 was actually F11's cursor defect; on an F11+F15 stack (F11 5fe697aa + F15, 3 hunks hand-resolved) format.o builds under the benchmark recipe, F11 14/14 probes + repro-5 pass, F15 44 pass on the stack. STALE at next phext refresh: tccgen.c Source scroll + Vol 3 segmentation (new member decl_excess), machines #2/#4 bindings, tccgen.c Design view, gate verdict.
- F17 LANDED LOCALLY (commit 0a2f66a7 on tip 1616004d, NOT pushed — wave-4 publish round): the .value gap closed as a full GAS data-directive family fix (audit measured on binutils 2.42 x86-64 ELF): aliases .value/.hword/.2byte/.4byte/.8byte/.zero; gen_expr16/gen_expr8 for width-2/1 symbol/difference/pcrel operands; .float/.single/.double with GAS flonum grammar (base-prefix skip + decimal parse, sign defeats prefix, NaN all payload bits); align max-skip arg; .fill >32-bit truncation; digit-led directive names recovered from the lexer PPNUM. .half/.xword documented non-implementations (GAS rejects both on this target); .uleb128/.sleb128/.dc noted gaps. Probes 58/61 byte+reloc identical (3 = pre-existing reloc-style class, baseline .long shows it too); float battery 16/16; ghash .rodata identical, .text stream 1130/1130 modulo F12 classes A-D. HEADLINE: OpenSSL 4.1.0 asm+shared builds COMPLETELY 2183/2183 (tip: 2181), apps/openssl runs, SHA-256 KAT exact, AES/HMAC/RSA/GCM KATs exact (no-tests configure: no suite to run). make test ALL PASSED; conformance unchanged 328/333. STALE: Source scrolls + Vol 3 + Design views for tccasm.c/tcctok.h/i386-asm.c/tcc.h + gate verdict.
- PQ-18 recon (2026-11-07): mechanism pinned to binary evidence + source; fix sized small-and-safe (F22 candidate). Report: ~/workspace/phcc-pq18/REPORT.md.
- F18 (PQ-17) FIXED, local commit 94a5fcd3 on 9d070f26, not pushed (wave-5 stack): _Static_assert evaluates at 64-bit width (do_Static_assert via expr_const64, tccgen.c +2/-2). Coreutils 9.12 builds completely, wc reproduces 1200000 13200000 166768523; sed/grep make check exit 0 incl. gnulib-tests (222 / 257 pass, 0 fail); make test ALL PASSED; conformance 328/333 unchanged.
- F23 (PQ-21) FIXED 2026-11-07, local commit 10014a50 (ranch branch pq21-dead-loop-suppression, NOT pushed; wave-5 publish is central): dead loops resurrected at the loop head (head gind() clears CODE_OFF_BIT) — FFmpeg's 16 phantom ff_* refs. Fix: label-aware token save/scan/replay in tccgen.c (+92); labelled/unbraced loops parse as base (87_dead_code passes byte-exact). Verified: make test ALL PASSED, conformance 328/333 baseline five, F13 corpus unchanged; FFmpeg on F20+F23 stack builds completely, transcode byte-matches gcc oracle fe93761b…. Report ~/workspace/phcc-pq21/REPORT.md.
- WAVE 5 PUBLISHED 2026-11-07 (subagent 968ad9ac): wbic16/phcc main == exo == 32674fc3, stacked on 9d070f26, no force: F18 5b09de54 (PQ-17), F19 0991ea07 (PQ-20), F20 450d24ec (PQ-19), F21 e1b6f896 (.note.GNU-stack), F22 cd4e1787 (PQ-18), F23 0ed6a84e (PQ-21), analyze 4f8c604e, stmt-tier 32674fc3 (34f5e672 appended per follow-up, stack unpushed at the time). PATCHES.md union: F1-F23 entries each exactly once, delta rows = base + per-fix increments in the file's own accounting convention (tccgen +425/-18 incl. publisher reconciliation of F23's omitted row update, +92/-0 from its own entry; tcc.h +69/-3; libtcc.c +63/-2; tccelf.c +1080/-17; x86_64-link.c new +7/-1); table order canonical. Exact-union proven semantically per file: tccgen F18 14/14 probes differential vs gcc + F23 23/23 shapes byte-equal undefined sets; tccelf F19 flagged first-wins both orders, F20 sysctl refused w/ compat error + memcpy runs, F21 GNU ld 0 warning bytes + PT_GNU_STACK RW, F22 mpfr gate reproducer A-E + 1.414213562373095 rc 0 (+ gawk -M smoke). Verification on stacked tree (aletheia-core): build rc 0, make test ALL PASSED (87_dead_code.c in run), conformance 328/333 agree 325+3, diverge set exactly baseline five, oracle splits 0. Fresh clone from GitHub: tip 32674fc3, F1-F23 once each, make test ALL PASSED. OpenSSL headline REPRODUCED: clean tree, Configure CC=stack no-tests, make build_sw rc 0, exactly 2,183 objects, apps/openssl 4.1.0, SHA-256('abc') KAT exact, PT_GNU_STACK RW.
- CORRECTION + NEW QUEUE ITEM PQ-24: the FFmpeg headline is NOT reproduced from a clean tree, and F23's 'FFmpeg builds completely' verification does not hold up. Clean build (gate recipe verbatim, stacked tcc): configure HAVE_SYSCTL 0 (F20 works), all 1,903 units compile, final link FAILS with 132 unresolved ff_hscale*/ff_yuv2plane* refs in libswscale/x86/swscale.o. Evidence the stack is faithful and the earlier claim was the defect: stacked tcc and F23's own tree produce IDENTICAL undefined sets on the decisive TU (156 ff_ total / 132 hspace+yuv2plane); base = 221, so F23 is a real but PARTIAL fix (loop-head shapes). gcc -O0 on the same command: 2 undefineds, 0 phantom (oracle folds). F23's build tree was configured under a different compiler (CONFIG_PIC/HAVE_INT128/HAVE_EBP_AVAILABLE all 1 - impossible under tcc) and its swscale.o carries the oracle profile (2 undefineds) with NO definitions of the hscale symbols anywhere in its archive - the completion rested on inherited artifacts, not a clean build. PQ-24: dead-branch suppression does not reach the libswscale x86 template instantiations (non-loop-head shapes); FFmpeg gate status returns to blocked-at-final-link on this one TU.
- PQ-24 FIXED as F24 (local commit 6a0fd059 on tip 32674fc3, ranch branch pq24 in ~/phcc-pq24/tree, NOT pushed — central publish). Root cause: F23's scan_save_span() counted any identifier followed by ':' as a label; ternary arms are identifiers, so every loop whose saved span (body, while condition, or inner if condition) held an identifier-armed ?: forfeited suppression, and the loop head's gind() left the rest of the dead region unsuppressed too (the ASSIGN_VSCALEX switch leaked by poison). Fix (tccgen.c +19/-5): the scan tracks a pending-? count (';' resets it); case constants/bitfields still match conservatively; a real label after a ternary is still detected (shape w05 unchanged at base behaviour). Evidence: 39-shape matrix — all 15 leaking shapes to 0, all clean shapes unchanged; decisive TU undefineds 160 -> 6 == gcc -O0 source-level set (2 surviving ff_ refs are live HAVE_MMXEXT_INLINE code); phantom extract 0 ff_*; make test ALL PASSED (87_dead_code in run); conformance 328/333 baseline five, 0 splits; live controls 39/39 .text byte-identical + libavutil/eval.o whole-object identical. ACCEPTANCE, clean tree (distclean-verified, gate recipe verbatim, configured under the FIXED compiler — config.h: CONFIG_PIC 0, HAVE_INT128 0, HAVE_EBP_AVAILABLE 0, HAVE_SYSCTL 0): FFmpeg 9.0.2 builds completely, 1,999 objects, ffmpeg+ffprobe link, transcode SHA-256 fe93761b29c11da087d776ec86e4632acfa39643863c7d4c1abfd6939712f056 == gcc oracle. PATCHES.md amended in the same commit: F24 entry + errata inside F23's entry (its FFmpeg headline rested on a tree configured under a different compiler with inherited artifacts; verified scope = loop-head shapes + extract; F24's headline replaces it). Report: ~/workspace/phcc-pq24/REPORT.md; patch mirror f24-6a0fd059.patch. With F24, every gate cell is green except OpenSSL test/rsa_complex.c (documented class-(b) _Complex boundary).
- WAVE 6 PUBLISHED 2026-11-07: wbic16/phcc main == exo == d0659ba4ef6caa94c120ffd7366c75b3c44e4d67 — F24 (6a0fd059) cherry-picked clean onto verified-fresh 32674fc3, stacked tree byte-identical to the fix commit's tree; push was fast-forward on both refs, NO force. PATCHES.md on the stack: F1-F24 each exactly once, F23 errata in place, F24 entry present, tccgen.c delta row +444/-23. Stacked-tree receipts (aletheia-core ~/phcc-wave6/tree): build + make test ALL TESTS PASSED (87_dead_code in run); conformance 328/333 (agree 325 + agree_reject 3), baseline five, 0 splits; shapes s02 0 / w05 3 as specified. Decisive-TU stack-integrity check: swscale.c under the STACKED compiler (gate flags, clean configured tree) = 6 undefineds IDENTICAL to the F24 receipt, ff_ set == gcc -O0 source-level set; full clean-tree FFmpeg receipt stands on 6a0fd059 itself. Fresh-clone verify: tip, 24 entries 0 dup, make test ALL PASSED. FFmpeg's gate cell is now earned on clean evidence — the only non-green cell left in the matrix is OpenSSL rsa_complex.c (documented class-(b) _Complex).
- GATE v2 (2026-11-07, tip d0659ba4): publication gate GREEN — 11/11 build from clean trees, all matrix test cells pass (gnulib 222/0 + 257/0, git 706/706 + nine fuzz helpers, gawk+MPFR ALL TESTS PASSED, FFmpeg 1,999 objects + transcode byte-identical to gcc oracle, OpenSSL subsets 123/123 shared + 121/121 static PASS with rsa_complex the sole class-(b) exclusion). No new compiler defect. Report ~/workspace/phcc-gate/GATE-REPORT-v2.md, logs ~/workspace/phcc-gate/logs-v2/.
- D1 wave (2026-11-07, local commits on d0659ba4, not pushed): F25 (ad911698) PQ-13 duplicate strong bss definitions error at object load; F26 (164c8ea4) PQ-23 static symbol closure (__ehdr_start + GCC runtime archives) with the static-IFUNC runtime-relocation residue measured into Wave D2; phext refresh (8413d6f5) brings the canonical phext to the F6-F26 source set (4ba5c6d3, 63,990 scrolls, gate v8.1.0).
- WAVE D1 PUBLISHED 2026-11-07: wbic16/phcc main == exo == 8413d6f50afac0c982466d05bb244892f533d2f1 — ad911698 (F25) -> 164c8ea4 (F26) -> 8413d6f5 (phext refresh) stacked on fresh-verified d0659ba4 (remote refs re-checked immediately before stacking; the ranch stack's parent chain already sat exactly on d0659ba4, so the published commits are the D1 commits themselves), push exo then fast-forward main, NO force. Verification on the stacked tree (aletheia-core ~/phcc-d1/tree, clean rebuild): build rc 0, make test ALL TESTS PASSED; conformance spot (fresh runner pass, binary stamp main@8413d6f5) 328/333 — agree 325 + agree_reject 3, diverges exactly the baseline five [a_pp_018, b_gnu_009, b_gnu_015, b_gnu_016, b_gnu_020], oracle splits 0. F25 spot: bs.o(bss marker) + d11.o(data marker) unflagged now LINK-FAILs 'defined twice' rc 1 (ld: multiple definition); flagged -Wl,--allow-multiple-definition links both orders with first-wins (marker=0 / marker=11). F26 receipts: tcc -static hello links rc 0 with ZERO unresolved (nm: 0 undefined); executing that glibc-static binary SEGFAULTS (rc 139, core dumped) — exactly the known IFUNC residue in F26's entry, reported not fixed; freestanding -static -nostdlib __ehdr_start probe RUNS: prints EHDR-OK, exit 0; static phccbox final link (phccbox11+sed+grep+awk+sh+bzip2+gzip+coreutils bundles, -lselinux -lpcre2-8 -lm -lgmp -lcrypto) completes rc 0, 11,592,364 B static ELF (link completion only, not executed). PATCHES.md on the stack: F1-F26 each exactly once (26 entries, verified by grep + fresh clone). Refresh integrity: phcc.phext SHA-256 4ba5c6d3b828df8bdb9df1b77f18dec1b4880aa436f4447feea54a81ad490104 and seal 1f9f1106e634c7ae5e83206cc166ed7e3676e5724b28e963d0267bf8a933e92d match the refresh commit; unpack from the published phext reproduces the stacked tree 608/608 byte-identical (0 mismatches; by-name exclusions phcc.phext/phcc.phext.xz/phcc-manifest.tsv/phext/** as documented in tools/METHODS.md). Fresh-clone verify from GitHub