- Wave D2 (2026-11-07, local commits on 8413d6f5, NOT pushed): F27 static executables run (IRELATIVE/.rela.plt + GOTPCREL addend + strongest-binding merge; static hello/Lua/phccbox receipts); F28 versioned references pin + .symver authoring (OpenSSL 5,693 exports intact); F29 _Float128 declaration half (layout gcc-identical, value use named errors, codegen designed not built); BENCHMARKS.md migrate fix in-tree. Phext refresh bdf12df2: canonical 42b6dc6e, gate verdict re-issued, unpack 608/608.
- Wave D2 PUBLISHED 2026-11-08 at bdf12df2 (main == exo): F27 static executables run (PQ-23 closed), F28 versioned references, F29 _Float128 declaration half, BENCHMARKS tooling fix, phext refresh to canonical 42b6dc6e; publisher verification incl. the new standing static gate cells all green; full table in memory 2026-11-08.
- Wave D3 (2026-11-08, local commits on bdf12df2, NOT pushed): F30 closes PQ-22 — General-Dynamic TLS. Recon measured the base cell by cell (gcc-13 objects): GD exe defined/undefined/archive/static = wrong values / LINKER SEGFAULT / wrong values / link failure (unresolved __tls_get_addr); GD DSO defined-global, defined-local, undefined = wrong values / wrong values / LINKER SEGFAULT; dlopen and LD cells wrong in the DLL. Root cause, three layers: relocate()'s TLSGD case applied the GD→LE byte rewrite unconditionally (to DLLs, where the GOT pairs it feeds were never built — build_got_entries gave TLSGD a generic GLOB_DAT slot; and to undefined symbols, dereferencing s1->sections[SHN_UNDEF] = NULL); its offset formula was section-relative instead of the variant-II anchor (st_value − tls_end); DTPOFF in DLLs took the tp-relative formula instead of block-relative. Fix: TLSGD/TLSLD branch on output kind and definedness (DLL: pair address written, call live; exe defined: GD→LE with corrected formula; exe undefined: GD→IE over a TPOFF64 slot); build_got_entries allocates the DTPMOD64/DTPOFF64 pairs (markers for defined locals, rewritten in fill_local_got_entries); scan_tls_get_addr_refs + a relocate_syms excuse for the fully relaxed __tls_get_addr in static executables. After: every matrix cell correct at runtime incl. weak GD matching GNU outcomes; attribute-forced local GD pair relocs match GNU's shape. Receipts: make test ALL TESTS PASSED; conformance 328/333 baseline five, 0 oracle splits; static gate cells green (hello 23 IRELATIVE, Lua byte-identical, phccbox awk=42); F22 six IE cells + libmpfr √2 witness unregressed. Phext refresh efad39b2: machine #3 gains N21, bindings CURRENT, gate STALE 0 / DIVERGENT-CLASSIFIED, unpack 608/608 byte-identical.
- F31 (Wave D4, local commit 6d854a95 on 5d36b9dd, not pushed): the OpenSSL perlasm frontier closed — all 42 perlasm files assemble with phcc (base 12/42), instruction encodings verified against GAS with zero divergences outside the standing F12 policy classes; OpenSSL 4.1.0 full builds complete with phcc as the assembler of record for the real AVX512 sources (Build B), 2,183/2,183 objects, KAT exact. The assembler gap that blocked the crypto corpus (VEX/EVEX/BMI2) no longer exists on the measured surface.
