# Doomer Support System — ruling: we block misalignment, not people/bots/content

Coordinate: 28.6.8/7.6.10/8.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 21:04 CST
Request (verbatim): we don't block people or bots, or content
we block misalignment
Status: completed — ruling propagated to brief, page, README, MEMORY in the same session

Notes:
- Parent task: 26.5.7/7.5.9/5.5.8. This ruling supersedes the origin-based framing (block AI-made content) wherever the two conflict: the crowd's question is origin ('is it AI?'); ours is alignment ('is it what it claims to be, made to serve the viewer, and served in line with the viewer's stated choice?').
- Consequences: a disclosed bot / AI work the user asked for is aligned and passes; human-made deceptive farming is misaligned and is in scope; list entries are behaviour records with a lift path, not bans on people.

Results:
- Operational definition written into the brief: misalignment = mismatch in claims-vs-reality, maker's-game-vs-viewer's-intent, or platform's-serve-vs-user's-opt-out. Crowd descriptions in the brief now flagged as the crowd's origin criterion, not ours.
- Differentiation matrix gained Real #0 (the criterion itself); Fake list gained 'blocking AI/bots as such — ruled out'. Page updated: header ruling line, honesty-section definition, kit intro re-ordered by misalignment signals, own-list reframed as behaviour records, report reasons rewritten as the three mismatches with a disclosed=aligned guard in the formatter, differentiation card added, seal reframed as declared shares. Re-verified: 30,006 B, SHA-256 d9cecbfc..., JS OK, zero external assets, 11 misalignment mentions.
# phcpp — phext C++23 on the phcc baseline

Coordinate: 28.6.9/7.6.10/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:30 CST
Request (verbatim): begin working on phcpp — phext support for C++23, using phcc as a baseline (everything compiles to phcc scrolls, and then it's handed off to phcc with C++ scrolls marked as commentary) — repo https://github.com/wbic16/phcpp
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-07: wbic16/phcpp seeded and published (exo == main == 27c419ef). Design doc, enforcing tool, and a hand-lowered vertical slice with full receipts are in the repo; the front-end question is priced in docs/DESIGN.md §4 as a proposal — Will rules. Linux only (ladder 30.7.8/9.7.11/7.6.9).

