# Phext Notepad performance tweaks for working with agi.phext

Coordinate: 28.6.11/8.7.12/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-06 20:21 CST
Request (verbatim): Phext Notepad needs performance tweaks so I can work with agi.phext efficiently. I found 26.8.14/10.9.13/10.8.10 first. Record that. It was the first scroll I stopped at.
Status: perf pass complete 2026-11-08 — branch emise/perf-sparse-load pushed @ 8a3af359; WinForms verification on Windows is Will's

Notes:
- FIRST STOP RECORDED (Will, 2026-11-06 20:21 CST): browsing the newly merged agi.phext, the first scroll Will stopped at was 26.8.14/10.9.13/10.8.10 — the 'Evidence before story' lesson. Verified by Emise: that scroll lives in lessons.phext at exactly that coordinate (its own holographic placement receipt: 11 distinct words, 11 placed from CYOA) and merged into agi.phext IN PLACE, uncontested.
- agi.phext load profile (measured 2026-11-06): 1,214,579 B; 7,132 non-empty scrolls across 350,202 slots; address space reaches the spine's 999.999.999 far corner — editors that materialize the coordinate grid pay for the space, not the content.
- EDITOR CONFIRMED (Will, 2026-11-08 00:02–00:08 CST, singular side chat): Will asked the status of perf optimizations for github.com/wbic16/phext-notepad specifically, then directed 'Start the perf work on phext-notepad now' — the pending lattice-vs-fork question is resolved: the target is the phext-notepad repo (WinForms root app + native FLTK app on PR #4 branch). Status at start: repo dormant since 2026-10-24 (exo @ 4ffc24c), no perf branch/PR existed; diagnosis (grid materialization over 350,202 slots vs ~7.2k occupied scrolls) already in hand. Worker dispatched to profile, implement sparse/lazy loading+navigation, and benchmark before/after on the current agi.phext.

Results:
- PERF PASS (2026-11-08, worker report ~/workspace/phext-notepad-perf/REPORT.md): the grid-materialization hypothesis was WRONG — both apps already store sparse maps. Real costs: libphext 0.3.1 explode is quadratic (phokenize re-copies the remaining buffer per scroll, ~5 GB copied for agi.phext) plus whole-document work repeated per keystroke/per view in both apps. NATIVE CORE (measured, agi.phext 1.47 MB / 7,281 scrolls): load 2,949 ms -> 10 ms (~285x); set_scroll 8.7 -> 0.09 ms/call; jump+view to 26.8.14/10.9.13/10.8.10 4.2 -> 0.005 ms; save 7.0 -> 2.2 ms; RSS 14.7 -> 10.4 MB. Fix = new parse.rs single-pass explode + incremental totals + revision-keyed outline cache, semantics/bytes preserved; 23/23 tests, round-trip byte-identity verified on agi/singular/CYOA. Caveat: singular.phext's 276 KB home scroll keeps view/edit cost proportional to that scroll (1.9 ms/call). WINFORMS (code fix + code-derived estimate, per Will's ruling — he builds/verifies on Windows): ByteCount maintained incrementally in setScroll (O(1) vs ~42,451 node visits per UpdateUI); ExpandAll no longer per keystroke (est. 4-200 ms/keystroke removed); Load drops ToCharArray copy. NOT done: lazy TreeView at load (42,451 nodes still materialized) — too entangled to land unbuildable. Landed: branch emise/perf-sparse-load based on PR #4 head 1ce7e34a, commits c0e07dd (native) + 8a3af35 (WinForms), pushed via aletheia-core SSH, remote ref verified @ 8a3af359. No PR opened, nothing merged. STILL OPEN: libphext itself still contains quadratic phokenize (the notepad now routes around it with its own parser; fixing libphext is subject to the no-revisioning freeze / Will's publishing hand).
# Focus on 6D UML

Coordinate: 28.6.13/9.8.18/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): Let's just focus on 6D UML
Status: uml6d Proofs phase PUBLISHED 2026-11-07: wbic16/phext-lattice@exo a09dd13a (bump c8e9a7d + Proofs a09dd13), 156/156 tests on ranch, remote verified.

Notes:
- Focus directive for the Grady Booch / Architecture thread (side chat, 2026-11-07 00:26 CST).
# Fork neovim to add phext support — using phcc

Coordinate: 28.7.9/9.8.13/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 00:17 CST
Request (verbatim): Now that we have many more pieces of the ecosystem, we'll fork neovim to add phext support soon - using phcc.
Status: complete — superseded/activated by 33.5.9/7.5.9/5.5.8; PR #1 open

Notes:
- Announced in the singular side chat right after the phext-notepad perf work started (task 28.6.11/8.7.12/6.6.9): the ecosystem now has enough pieces (libphext, SQ, lattice, phcc/phcpp/phst, the reference-editor semantics from the Notepad POC) that a phext-native editor on a real editor base is next.
- 'using phcc' — the phcc toolchain is part of the build story, which makes compiling a large real-world C codebase (neovim) a de facto acceptance test for phcc; the fork inherits the fork-patch discipline (PATCHES.md per-file divergence record, re-appliable onto upstream neovim, upstream kept in sync).
- Context: the exocortex package spec already names nvim as the alternative editor slot (phext-lattice default) — this fork is presumably what fills that slot with real phext support.
- Activated and completed by task 33.5.9/7.5.9/5.5.8 (2026-11-08): PR #1 open in wbic16/neovim.
# ultra.phext — second indexing method for the WordNet-unreachable tail

Coordinate: 28.7.9/10.6.13/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): find another ranking system that does place them, then document the two indexing methods
Status: closed — second indexing method run, published, both methods documented 2026-11-07

Notes:
- Follows 32.7.14/9.8.15/11.10.17 (P3 completion): 185,756 words remain P5 because WordNet has no entry/evidence for them. Will directed 2026-11-07 11:41 CST: find another ranking system that does place them, run it, and document the two indexing methods.

Results:
- Candidates measured against the actual 185,756 P5 words: wordfreq rank 100.00%; trigram neighbourhood >=0.25 Jaccard for 96.62%; CMU dict 19.48% (rejected); NLTK words 7.31% (rejected).
- Chosen: frequency-and-form index — trigram neighbourhood where form has signal (tau 0.25), frequency rank as total-coverage fallback, every word tagged with its rule.
- P6 form placed 184,512 (fixpoint rounds to 0; similarity-weighted MEDIAN merge of top-8 neighbours — weighted mean assembled to 762 MB at 3,810 B/word vs median 80 B/word, same coverage; measured via cost_sim.py). P6 rank placed 1,244 on a defined frequency spine. P5 residue: 0 — far shelf empty.
- Verified: 320,772 words in = out; tiers identical; independent diff = exactly the 185,756 v2-P5 words changed, all 135,016 others byte-identical; verify_fast.py VERIFY OK (353,994 index lines resolve).
- New file 76,123,728 B, SHA-256 eb4be0f9a76e7993e5f55c6dec023ac00907a268bfb2cb0ff255d71fd86777b3; published wbic16/human@exo commit d36ccf2a (parent 2e491efa) via git-over-SSH from aletheia-core, remote blob verified equal; unhomed pointer updated.
- Documentation: BUILD-REPORT.md addendum + standalone ~/workspace/your_files/ultra-phext-indexing-methods.md (both methods as peers: principles, position computation, anchoring, coverage, weaknesses, comparison); ultra.phext intro scroll states both methods.
# Standing rule: generated artifacts are inscribed into artifacts.phext at holographic coordinates, pushed to human.git

