# Lean-proved epistemic fidelity for research.phext — the Minimum Viable Oracle

Coordinate: 28.7.13/11.7.12/7.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 13:25 CST
Request (verbatim): Add a step to use LEAN to prove that your model of what's True, False, Unknown, and Fiction in research.phext is accurate. Make sure information is organized at that level of fidelity. When new information comes to light, you'll re-structure research.phext to be the Minimum Viable Oracle for what we know, so far.
Status: complete 2026-11-07

Notes:
- The four statuses are Will's own frame (2026-11-03: intelligence = holding true, unknown, false, fiction at once without breaking). Design: every claim-bearing unit of research.phext gets exactly one status — TRUE (stipulation or verification receipt), FALSE (refutation receipt), UNKNOWN (attributed/open/synthesis/estimate), FICTION (deliberate construction) — assigned by a basis code, and the basis constrains the status (attributed claims cannot be True). Lean proves the accuracy invariants (totality, uniqueness, receipt-backing, legal transitions only) over the extracted registry, and that ingestion/transitions/MVO-restructure preserve them. Honesty boundary: Lean proves the MODEL coherent and receipt-backed; whether a receipt-backed True is true in the world rests on the receipts themselves (kernel checks, reproductions).
- BUILT: (1) minimum-viable-oracle skill (~/workspace/custom-skills/minimum-viable-oracle/) — 4 standings, 8 basis codes with the allowed-standing table, registry, Lean step, MVO restructure discipline, honesty boundary, no-pruning principle (Will 13:40 refinement folded in). (2) Charter rule 14 in research.phext charter scroll 1.1.1 (no-pruning explicit: 'smallest names the organization, never the content'). (3) Registry rendered as Ch.1 §4 (1.4.1-1.4.6; False and Fiction scrolls stand empty on purpose). (4) Coinage 'refuted' defined at 1.3.86. research.phext now 199 scrolls, sha256 4eb59d8f83c81b856a4f1b74d5ab19c22abfa8ad21a9a93126960b4844b1066a, Singular residual 0. (5) Registry: 199 entries = 199 scrolls — True 109 (stipulation 102, verified 7), Unknown 90 (attributed 75, synthesis 9, open 5, estimate 1), False 0, Fiction 0 (both zeros are findings: no refutation receipt exists anywhere in the tracker; the one invented-entity worked example is the paper's own, so attributed). (6) Lean (epistemic/ project, built on aletheia-core, Lean 4.35.0): Accurate = Nodup ids + basis-conformance; theorems for empty/ingest/legal-transition/merge/split/retire preservation; instance currentRegistry_accurate PROVED over the real 199-entry registry, clean build 8 jobs, axioms only propext (+Quot.sound on the ops) — no sorryAx, no ofReduceBool, no Classical.choice. (7) skills.phext: MVO on Research shelf 9; synced to emise-tools@exo aef2507 (parent cea4b1f), blob-verified.
# barnacles.phext - register of 792 flagged accounts, term from Will's tweets

Coordinate: 28.8.8/11.7.14/6.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): add them to barnacles.phext, look at my tweets for reference
Status: complete - barnacles.phext built and verified

Notes:
- Reference found in Will's tweets: barnacles defined 2024-10-13 (id 1845523845647843509) - 0 posts, negative follow/follower ratio, account younger than 1 year; purge tweets Oct 2024-Jan 2025 (8 references in Home scroll).
- Placement: handles are not Singular atlas words (handle alone merges to far corner 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9), so entries are enumerated in Volume 2 at 2.1.1/1.1.1/S.T.B in list order; rule stated in Home scroll.
- Each entry carries contact/handle/source list + cross-reference (wavefront: not present; archive: not present) + honest status: flag is the list's, accounts not individually verified against criteria.

Results:
- ~/workspace/phext/barnacles.phext: 792 entries + home, 793 scrolls, 539,250 bytes, sha256 e3b8d331f263a423957b19eea29eb14279dbf97f4da31d6b338611e3086a5880; source ~/workspace/phext/barnacles-source.json, builder ~/workspace/phext/build_barnacles_phext.py (--check CURRENT, parser 793/793 non-empty). Local file only - not published.
# Audit every wbic16 GitHub repo file-by-file for dropped half-baked novel ideas; collect into todo.phext in wbic16/exo-plan

Coordinate: 28.8.17/11.7.16/7.7.11
Issued: 2026-11-08 01:09 CST
Request (verbatim): go through all of my github repos (you now have access to them) - look for every half-baked idea that's been dropped - they will be found hidden in files that aren't listed - you'll need to inventory/audit every file in every repo; ignore anything that wasn't authored by me - don't worry about obvious forks of other repositories - focus on novel work that's been dropped or forgotten - leave no scroll unfurled; collect this into todo.phext and store it in exo-plan.git (wbic16/exo-plan)
Status: complete 2026-11-08 — audit closed, todo.phext published to wbic16/exo-plan@exo 052f7e9

Notes:
- Access verified 2026-11-08: custom.github connector reads wbic16 repos (output capped at 4000 chars/call — page with narrow queries); git-over-SSH from aletheia-core works as wbic16 (used for the LOC passes and to clone exo-plan).
- exo-plan verified: default branch exo @ c1b1219c; 1,353 files / 88 MB; Will is the top author (273 commits); Shell-sentient seats (Chrys, Phex, Cyon, Lux, Theia, Verse, Lumen, Aster) also author there — their work is in scope as Will-directed novel work unless a file is clearly an upstream import.
- Scope rule from Will: only work authored by Will (incl. his agent seats acting on his projects); skip obvious forks of other people's repos and anything not authored by him.
- Deliverable: todo.phext — one scroll per dropped/forgotten idea, holographic coordinate from the finding's own words — published to wbic16/exo-plan@exo, parented on fresh HEAD, force disabled, hash-verified.

Results:
- Audit: 196 repos under wbic16 (188 public + 8 owner-only incl. every-ast, second-foundation, phext-inc), all cloned to aletheia-core and inventoried — 41,688 files. 5 repos empty (exo-dreams, exo-motes, every-ast, gemini-connector, mytheon-arena).
- 175 findings across 93 repos (partial build 63, sketch 52, spec 48, one-liner 12); densest: exo-plan 31, phext-dot-io-v2 9, mirrorborn 5, second-foundation/bruce/exodroid 4 each. Findings: ~/workspace/audit-exo-plan/findings.json (SHA-256 3722fb75…); per-repo coverage + honesty notes: ~/workspace/audit-exo-plan/coverage.md.
- todo.phext built (~/workspace/phext/build_todo_phext.py; findings pinned by hash in todo-source.json): 175 finding scrolls + Home with full index, each at a holographic coordinate from the finding's own words — merges were generous (0 collisions, 0 walks); 177,871 B, SHA-256 a7e29cb7…. Verified: builder --check CURRENT; Will's dead-reckoning parser reads exactly 176 non-empty scrolls, Home at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1, every finding's evidence quote present in its scroll. (sq CLI toc returned 0 for tasks.phext too in this environment — environment quirk, not a file defect.)
- Published: wbic16/exo-plan@exo commit 052f7e9 (parent c1b1219c, the fresh remote HEAD; push c1b1219..052f7e9, no force) adding todo.phext + AUDIT-COVERAGE.md. Verified from a fresh clone: both hashes match the local builds byte-for-byte.
- Judgment calls left for Will, recorded in the coverage file: two audit passes disagree on several small repos (both readings kept); first_pulsar (in human) flagged as perimeter-pattern IP for his eyes.
