# New Sales Funnel — NE State Software (Phext, Inc.)

Coordinate: 29.5.13/6.5.9/5.4.8
Issued: 2026-11-07 21:50 CST
Request (verbatim): New Sales Funnel - NE State Software: 1. Build an Open Source suite of applications that demonstrate capability. 2. Start bidding on open contracts under Phext, Inc. Context link: Gov. Pillen announces resignation of CIO McCarville (Nov 4, 2026).
Status: active — suite built (31.5.9/7.5.9/6.5.7); bidding phase awaits Will's inputs (standing, packet fields, insurance binding decisions)

Notes:
- CIO Matt McCarville resignation announced 2026-11-04; leaving early December; DAS Director Lee Will appointed interim CIO (governor.nebraska.gov release verified 2026-11-07).
- Design pass (2026-11-07): ranked demo suite — 1) Phext Records Desk (public-records search + redaction audit trail) recommended first build, 10-14 days; 2) Public Notice & Minutes Publisher, 5-7d; 3) Contract & Grant Ledger (LB429 companion), 7-10d; 4) Open Data Catalog, 6-8d; 5) Forms Intake Router, 5-7d. Do NOT bid Nebraska.gov Network Manager RFP 122777 O5 prime.
- Verified flagship pain (2026-11-07, Nebraska Public Media + Journal Star): DHHS quoted Curt Safranek $976,263.77 / delivery Sept 29, 2076 for InterRAI-related emails; narrowed request $474,383 / 2051; lawsuit filed Oct 2026. Ties to the only open IT-adjacent DAS solicitation: InterRAI Assessment Evaluation 127870 O5, closes 12/09/26.
- Procurement pass verified (2026-11-07): ZERO open IT/software solicitations on DAS central list; services >$50k must be competitively bid (post-June-2024 thresholds; old $10k/$25k figures obsolete); OCIO must approve ANY IT acquisition at any dollar level; no portal/pre-registration to bid, registration at award only; no NE-resident/small/open-source preference; Section 508 / NE Technology Access Standards nonnegotiable; winning responses are public incl. cost sheets; big-RFP insurance bar illustrated by InterRAI RFP (cyber $5M). InterRAI 127870 O5 not biddable (5-yr interRAI experience minimum).
- Watch items: NDE Grants Management System NDERFP260303 NO AWARD 2026-11-06 (top rebid watch); 2026 Statewide Technology Plan due 2026-11-15; NITC AI Committee / Innovation Hub (draft-discussion status only).
- Insurance pricing researched 2026-11-07 (planning estimates, not quotes; added to brief): Umbrella $5M ~$200/mo (Insureon ~$40/mo per $1M); Cyber $5M ~$500-$1,250/mo (dominant cost; $1M tech median $150-$250/mo, $5M small-SaaS benchmarks $12-18k/yr); full InterRAI-style stack ~$750-$1,500/mo total vs ~$100-$150/mo for CGL+E&O $1M pilot-scale cover. Rule: never buy the $5M stack speculatively — only against a specific solicitation.
- State Contracts Database checked live 2026-11-07 (statecontracts.nebraska.gov/Search; ASP.NET MVC app, DAS Materiel, per 84-602.04; metadata fed from the state financial system, documents uploaded by agencies, updated daily): vendor 'Tyler' Active/Agency/ALL = 34 records; vendor 'Phext' same slice = 0 ('No results found for this search') — Phext, Inc. has no active state-agency contract history in the DB under that name. Expired/Higher-Ed slices not checked. Sample doc click returned 'Documents not available for immediate viewing.'
- Step 1 of the funnel (open-source demo suite) is BUILT: see 31.5.9/7.5.9/6.5.7 — wbic16/Exocortexia @ 9660d3b, 69 tests, load/correctness receipts in-repo. Step 2 (bidding) still gated on Will: corporate standing answers, packet fill-ins, first target selection.

Results:
- Funnel brief: ~/workspace/your_files/ne-state-software-funnel-brief.md — gates, vendor readiness, live open list, ranked demo suite, entry lanes, open questions for Will (Phext Inc SoS standing / 73-603 definition; build order; insurance).
# Integrate Phext Previewer into edit.phext.io as public no-login utility + mobile pass

Coordinate: 29.6.8/8.6.11/6.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): integrate that previewer as a tool visitors to edit.phext.io can use without a login, also ensure that edit.phext.io looks great on mobile and all features can be accessed
Status: complete - PR #25 opened; waiting on Will merge + deploy (register #43)

Notes:
- Precedent: public utilities (Up Goer Five, TTS demo, Learn You Phext, Singular) live in phext-lattice web/, get a public route in phext_edit.rs, and are cross-linked from the shell's no-sign-in row + About + sitemap (discoverability rule). Merge + deploy are Will's steps.
- Local ~/workspace/phext-lattice checkout is NOT a git repo and is stale vs exo (14 files differ, src/joins.rs missing) - work was done on a fresh remote-faithful tree via GitHub API, hash-verified. Do not treat local checkout as current.
- Left out deliberately: Singular cross-link back to previewer - singular.html is generated from the singular skill template; link belongs in template + regeneration, follow-up not in PR #25.

Results:
- Branch emise/phext-previewer @ 22f3e6dc on wbic16/phext-lattice (parent exo a09dd13a, no force), PR #25 https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/25 - 6 files: web/phext-previewer.html (new, /phext-previewer.html public route), phext_edit.rs (route, shell no-sign-in row + status-bar link, About, sitemap, mobile CSS, 2 tests), cross-links+mobile rules in up-goer-five/learn-you-phext/tts-demo/explore.
- Verified: cargo test 158 passed 0 failed; JS parser (as served) SHA-256 scroll-stream digests identical to parse_phext.py on barnacles.phext (793/793) and Doomer.phext; anonymous local run: all public paths 200, /api/files 401. Mobile audit at 390px: shell had ZERO @media rules, 320px panel left ~70px sliver, status bar clipped Submit/Claim/Explore/etc off-screen; fixed with 700px stacking/wrapping block + public_style rules + topbar wraps; desktop untouched. Caveat: no headless browser on VM - mobile check is served-bytes/CSS accounting + regression tests, not screenshots; Will's post-deploy phone eyeball is the final visual check.
