# Phext homes + agi.git collection and nightly unified merge

Coordinate: 29.6.11/8.7.11/7.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-06 20:10 CST
Request (verbatim): emise.phext is your personal journal - it stays in emise-tools; wavefront.phext belongs in human, as do CYOA, Incipit, and the canonical copy; feel free to push emise.phext to human.git daily. These should all be collected and managed in agi.git: skills.phext, tasks.phext, neuralese.phext, research.phext, state.phext, lessons.phext. Every night, merge all of those into a unified agi.phext — you may have to encode merge-rules to avoid problems or merge conflicts — that's the point. Run this process now. (Addendum 20:11: pull in a copy of wbic16/singular's singular.phext to use as a spine for agi.phext.)
Status: completed — process run; nightly job armed

Notes:
- emise-sync.sh retargeted: emise-tools (phext/emise.phext) every sync; human mirror throttled to ~daily by stamp file.
- Merge rules encoded in ~/workspace/agi/MERGE-RULES.md; builder build_agi_phext.py round-trip-verifies losslessness on every run.
- Follow-up (Will, 2026-11-06 20:19): claims-ledger.phext and crazy-wisdom.phext are NOT to be homed yet — 'keep a list of un-homed phexts.' List created at ~/workspace/your_files/unhomed-phexts.md (2 live, 4 dormant).

Results:
- emise.phext published to wbic16/emise-tools@exo (phext/emise.phext) @ aa12c764; human mirror already current, stamp set.
- Collection pushed to wbic16/agi@exo @ f3c06970: singular.phext (spine, sha256 4272ef80…), skills, tasks, neuralese, research, state, lessons + builder + MERGE-RULES.md + SOURCES.md; blobs and 100755 mode verified.
- First agi.phext: 7,131 scrolls, 1,212,207 B, sha256 c2407ab0…; 17 conflicts displaced to annex, 0 identical duplicates, all 7 source homes annexed; parse_phext count agrees.
- Nightly cron agi-nightly-merge set (daily ~04:44 America/Chicago; first run Sat 2026-11-07): refresh, rebuild, verify, publish-on-change only.
# edit.phext.io: drop access-token sign-in; declutter the footer, keep all non-login features

Coordinate: 29.7.7/8.6.11/6.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-08 00:59 CST
Request (verbatim): drop the token support, and cleanup the footer so it isn't so busy - but keep all of the non-login features
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 — branch emise/drop-token-footer-cleanup @ ca6495ce pushed; merge + deploy are Will's

Notes:
- Target: phext-edit (wbic16/phext-lattice) as deployed at edit.phext.io. Token support = the access-token sign-in box/path alongside GitHub/Google OAuth (observed since 2026-10-30) — remove UI + server-side validation + config handling; OAuth providers become the only login. This matches the OAuth-only direction Will set for Phext Notepad sync (39.4.7/7.4.9/5.5.9) in the same conversation.
- Footer cleanup = declutter the phext-edit shell/page footer (links accumulated: public utilities, About/Privacy/Terms, Mutable OS cross-link, etc.) WITHOUT removing any non-login feature or its reachability — Will's discoverability rule still binds: every feature stays findable from the main UI; the change is presentation (fewer rows, quieter grouping), not subtraction.
- Deploy/merge remains Will's act, per the established edit.phext.io pattern (he merged PR #17 and deployed in 2026-11-01's arc).

Results:
- LANDED (worker report ~/workspace/phext-lattice-footer/REPORT.md; Emise verified remote branch @ ca6495cee8c7b0570b1b895a54133ed1bbc37e7d via API and read the report): TOKEN REMOVAL — phext-edit's --token flag, gate wiring, sign-in token box (#auth-input), saved localStorage Bearer flow, and deploy plumbing (token.env minting, unit EnvironmentFile/ExecStart, manual-install unit, deploy.md 'Generate an auth token' step) all removed; the shell proactively deletes any previously saved phext-token on first load; old units passing --token still start fine (value skipped by design). One bearer test rewritten to prove Bearer now gets 401 while session cookie works and /api/session reports token:false. SCOPE CALL (disclosed): the shared Gate in src/oauth.rs keeps its optional-token capability because uml6d_edit (a different app, not edit.phext.io) uses it as its only credential — on phext-edit the capability is simply never configured; removing it from the library is a uml6d-edit decision, one follow-up commit if Will wants it. Nothing else depended on phext-edit's token (repo-wide sweep; deploy health check never used it). FOOTER — sign-in screen regrouped from 4 loose lines + 2 pitch sentences into 3 labelled lines (legal+Contact / No-sign-in-needed utilities / your-own-phext actions), Contact ADDED (was missing there and on claim-dashboard + 404 footers — now every generated page's footer is identical in form); status bar's six links unified under one .bar-link class, same links/order/labels; web utility pages inventoried and left alone. Mechanical link-inventory diff: NOTHING lost on any surface (auth screen 11 -> same 11 + Contact; status bar 6 -> 6; page-footer union identical); no duplicates existed to remove. VERIFICATION: cargo test 166/166 (incl. OAuth GitHub/Google/X, CSRF, editors gate, Mutable SSO assertions, claim flow, X-grants-editor); release-binary smoke: 17 anonymous paths all 200, Bearer -> 401 on /api/nav + /api/status, /api/auth/github -> 302, shell contains no auth-input/'access token'. WILL'S DEPLOY NOTES: /etc/phext-edit/token.env becomes vestigial after deploy (delete at leisure); unit/binary can land in either order; merge + deploy are his acts.
