# 9D zooming UI — Twitter archive explorer

Coordinate: 29.8.11/10.8.15/7.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-06 18:20 CST
Request (verbatim): in addition to the video, let's build the 9D zooming UI that let's anyone explore their own Twitter archive in real-time
Status: completed — v1 delivered

Notes:
- Local-first: runs on the user's own archive, nothing uploaded. Demo dataset from Will's archive via Singular atlas math; upload mode parses tweets.js client-side.
- Full 46,719-word atlas bundled for upload mode (1.48 MB) — subsetting proved unnecessary, upload coordinates stay exact.
- Demo coordinates computed in float, rounded half-up only for phext display; uploaded archives are placed in Will's Singular dialect by design (his atlas).
- Coordinate math cross-checked Python vs in-browser over the whole archive: exact on 29,537/29,539 tweets (2 emoji variation-selector token-boundary cases; browser tokenizer uses Unicode letter classes to match the Singular checker).
- Hosted artifact's demo is 133 clearly-labelled sample tweets; the COMPLETE dataset (all 29,539 tweets + 1,822 people) is in the workspace standalone.html. Likes/DMs/followers excluded from v1.

Results:
- Workspace build: ~/workspace/wavefront/archive-explorer/ — index.html/style.css/app.js, build_demo_data.py, build_standalone.py, standalone.html (single file, 6.76 MB, opens from file://), data/demo.json (29,539 tweets + 1,822 people), data/atlas-full.json, README.md.
- Hosted artifact: slug 9d-archive-explorer — independently implemented, probe-verified live (word search flies to phext at 21.20.17/11.21.23/4.23.21; zoom descent, era chip, chronological Play, upload panel all pass; two defects found and fixed in verification).
