# Phext-native memory exploration + six WG14-style C proposal specs (bignum, PIC, BCD mode, threads, stacks, phext heaps)

Coordinate: 31.5.7/7.6.12/8.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): Explore phext-native memory management (cache architecture); six WG14-style C proposal specs: bignum, PIC layouts, BCD mode, native threads, developer-managed stacks, phext-addressed heaps.
Status: COMPLETE + corrected: set survived adversarial review (117 findings), all corrections applied 2026-11-07.

Notes:
- Will's direction, verbatim in substance: explore memory management from a phext-native perspective in light of modern cache architecture; imagine Will/Phext-shaped patches to C; formal spec per proposal, submittable to the C committee in theory.
- Honesty constraints: _BitInt (C23), _Decimal (C23), C11 threads, deprecated makecontext all exist and must be grappled with.

Results:
- Verified on disk: 00 (19,176 B), 01 (28,102 B), 02 (26,812 B), 03 (28,940 B), 04 (34,324 B), 05 (36,154 B), 06 (20,844 B) + INDEX.md.
# Build NE state portfolio suite in wbic16/Exocortexia + SSO + load/correctness + insurance/bidding packet

Coordinate: 31.5.9/7.5.9/6.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:00 CST
Request (verbatim): build those apps in https://github.com/wbic16/Exocortexia; Setup SSO with edit.phext.io; figure out a way to simulate load and prove correctness; put together an insurance and bidding packet
Status: completed 2026-11-07 — all agent-side steps done and verified. Remaining steps are Will's: merge phext-lattice emise/sso-exocortexia + set PHEXT_SSO_EXOCORTEXIA_URL + restart phext-edit (runbook); complete packet fill-in fields; broker quotes; any bid submission.

Notes:
- Parent funnel task: 29.5.13/6.5.9/5.4.8. Repo description: 'A proof of concept automated system for states with fewer than 5M residents'; MIT, (c) 2026 Will Bickford; initial commit ad1c827 contains only LICENSE.
- SSO precedent: edit.phext.io <-> Mutable SSO is LIVE (120s single-use HMAC assertion under dedicated PHEXT_SSO_SECRET; consumer sets own session cookie; pass-through when unconfigured). Suite SSO reuses that pattern; edit-side generalization + secrets + deploy are Will's steps (as with Mutable).
- Stack fixed by coordinator: Rust workspace (core phext store + hash-chained audit; sso crate on the Mutable pattern with mock minter; 5 apps; tools/loadsim; seed generators; docs incl. VERIFICATION.md with real run numbers). Builds/tests on aletheia-core, push via git SSH from there, branch exo, no force push.
- SSO edit-side: separate pass on phext-lattice branch emise/sso-exocortexia (allowlisted aud, mutable endpoint untouched); merge/deploy/secrets remain Will's steps. Runbook to ~/workspace/your_files/exocortexia-sso-deploy-runbook.md.
- SSO edit-side DONE + independently verified 2026-11-07: phext-lattice branch emise/sso-exocortexia @ 8660b05374 (parent exo c65f4d86); ls-remote confirms branch at that SHA, exo untouched. Endpoint generalized to GET /api/auth/sso/<aud> with allowlist (mutable, exocortexia); mutable flow is the same code path (no drift); unknown aud 404s before session handling; same PHEXT_SSO_SECRET, no new secret needed; exocortexia has NO default target — 404s until PHEXT_SSO_EXOCORTEXIA_URL is set (origin never guessed). Tests on aletheia-core: 162 passed, 0 failed (8 SSO tests: 4 old Mutable + 4 new). Not merged/deployed — Will's steps per runbook.
- Suite build DONE 2026-11-07 + independently verified by Emise: wbic16/Exocortexia exo @ 9660d3becd (4 commits over LICENSE-only ad1c827, 42 files; scripts/verify.sh mode 100755 in pushed tree). Emise's own fresh clone on aletheia-core re-ran cargo test --workspace: 69 passed, 0 failed (core 14, sso 10, seed 8, records-desk 4, minutes 7, ledger 8, catalog 7, forms 11) — matches builder's VERIFICATION.md. libphext 0.4.0 from crates.io (0.4.2 unpublished).
- Load/correctness receipts in repo docs/VERIFICATION.md: 100k-doc store — build 69ms, serialize 32.4MB/83ms, parse 94ms, 200 full-corpus searches 2,407ms, tamper negative control detected. HTTP 50 concurrent x 1,000 req, 0 errors, p95 1.1-15.2ms vs 500ms budget. REAL FAILURE found+fixed: at 500 concurrent, pre-fix p95 1,048ms FAILED budget (128-deep listen backlog) -> socket2 1024 backlog -> p95 26ms / p99 38ms / 0 errors.
- SSO consumer verified against mock edit-minter: full chain 200 + exo_session cookie; replay -> 401; tampered -> 401; unconfigured -> pass-through with AUTH DISABLED banner. Live minting waits on Will's edit-side steps (runbook). Known gaps: records-desk demo corpus 400 docs in-app (100k proven at store level); 2 benign warnings; load numbers are loopback on aletheia-core.
- SSO branch head moved: emise/sso-exocortexia now @ 122ff68e (wishnode audience added on the same branch, task 13.6.8/7.6.9/6.6.9); runbook updated accordingly. One merge still arms exocortexia (+wishnode).
- Post-build security pass (36.5.6/5.5.10/4.5.8) hardened the suite: exo now @ 342a268, 84 tests. Behavior changes affecting deployment: fail-closed SSO config, EXO_DEMO_MODE=1 for open mode, per-app audiences by default (set EXO_SSO_AUD=exocortexia for lattice-SSO deploys), 127.0.0.1 default bind, EXO_STATE_DIR persistence, EXO_AUDIT_KEY keyed audit chain.

Results:
- Insurance & bidding packet assembled: ~/workspace/your_files/ne-bidding-packet/ (00 index + fill-in fields, 01 vendor registration checklist, 02 broker-ready insurance quote packet, 03 capability statement, 04 proposal skeleton aligned to SPB scoring). Template state: bracketed Phext, Inc. fields await Will's data; nothing submitted.
- SSO deploy runbook: ~/workspace/your_files/exocortexia-sso-deploy-runbook.md (merge -> set PHEXT_SSO_EXOCORTEXIA_URL -> restart phext-edit -> GET health check (HEAD gives misleading 401) -> enable consumer; rollback = remove env line + restart).
- Repo: https://github.com/wbic16/Exocortexia @ exo 9660d3becd09b0348ac342e500eba44f1c7c4228 — 5 apps (records-desk 8801, minutes-publisher 8802, contract-ledger 8803, data-catalog 8804, forms-router 8805), exo-core + exo-sso crates, tools/loadsim, seed generators (deterministic; hashes in VERIFICATION.md), docs incl. statute sheets + SSO.md + API-CONTRACT.md.
# libphext-cs 0.5.0 parity: binary scrolls + xz seal (interop with Mutable)

Coordinate: 31.6.8/7.6.10/7.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 00:57 CST
Request (verbatim): yes, add that - so we can interop with mutable
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 — libphext-cs 0.5.0 landed on exo @ 27cb1a3a; READY for Will to package and push

Notes:
- 'That' = the cs 0.5.0 parity bump flagged at the close of 35.6.14/8.8.15/6.5.9: port libphext-rs 0.5.0's canonical binary scroll format + xz seal to libphext-cs so C#-side tooling can interop with Mutable (Mutable embeds media as binary scrolls in its phexts and ships xz seals; its stack is phext-lattice/libphext-rs).
- Canonical format (from rs PR #9, now in rs exo @ 0.5.0): binary scroll = header line 'phext-binary:1:base64' + newline + RFC 4648 base64 (padded, unwrapped); header alone = empty payload; header-prefixed scroll is binary BY DEFINITION; malformed binary scroll fetches verbatim; non-UTF-8 updates base64-encoded VERBATIM via byte-level insert/replace/ingest (phokenize_bytes), never rejected, never panics. xz seal: preset 6 over the whole phext, seal is transport/storage only, never the working format; any valid xz stream unseals.
- Decisive test = cross-implementation interop: fixtures produced by the real rs 0.5.0 crate must read byte-identically in cs, and cs output must verify in rs — both directions, binary scrolls and seals.
- Base: libphext-cs exo @ 85321e0f (0.4.0 + linear tokenizer). Version surface -> 0.5.0. NuGet publish remains Will's hand.

Results:
- LANDED + VERIFIED (worker report ~/workspace/libphext-cs-fix/REPORT-0.5.0.md; Emise independently re-verified remote exo SHA 27cb1a3a714c93e79c6aeaa910c18a1e886a4f80 + csproj <Version>0.5.0</Version> via API): BinaryScroll in the core assembly (canonical header/base64 format, InsertBinary/ReplaceBinary/FetchBinary, InsertBytes/ReplaceBytes/PhokenizeBytes/Ingest under base64-verbatim ingestion, PositionedByteScroll type; strict decode mirrors Rust STANDARD engine via re-encode canonical check because .NET base64 tolerates whitespace). Seal in a NEW companion assembly Phext.Seal over Joveler.Compression.XZ 5.0.2 (real liblzma, natives bundled win/linux/mac; preset 6 + CRC64, single-stream decode) — core stays dependency-free, mirroring the rs feature gate. P/Invoke rejected (no liblzma by default on Windows); SharpCompress is decode-only. Tests: cs 60/60 (45 regression + 10 binary + 5 seal ported 1:1 from rs; rs suite re-run 78/78 as reference). INTEROP HARNESS (mirror Rust+C# programs, one construction script): byte-identical on everything — constructed doc (empty / all-256-bytes / break-byte / 1 MiB+13 at scroll 1006 / malformed / namespace-claimed payloads), foreign-stream ingest, per-scroll manifests, 41-case decode-verdict battery, all five seals (agi.phext, CYOA, doc, empty, small); cross-unseal both directions; system xz -dc reproduces cs seals; cs unseals foreign seals at preset 0, 9e+SHA256, no-check, CRC32. Two porting defects caught+fixed en route (C# 'sealed' keyword; greedy \x escapes silently altering test content vs rs originals, rewritten as \u0017). WILL'S STEPS: optional tag v0.5.0 (only v0.3.0 exists remotely), then pack/push — NOTE the solution now yields TWO nupkgs (libphext-cs.0.5.0 + Phext.Seal.0.5.0) and scripts/publish.sh pushes only the core one; seal package needs its own push or a script tweak.
