Status: LANDED 2026-11-08: wave-boundary drift check confirmed upstream still at 70adbb12 (GitHub mirror and repo.or.cz HEAD/mob in parity; 0 commits past 70adbb12, exactly 1 past the old base). Landed stacked on the D3 publish (efad39b2): cherry-pick 8e012ad5 (zero conflicts, 4 files +29/−1), PATCHES U1 entry 96c47e93 (base pin c638ddf → 70adbb12; no F-number — not a fork patch), phext refresh 5d36b9dd (canonical ced9de67…, seal eccc43c3…, gate verdict 453110eb… re-issued and byte-idempotent, Design STALE 0, machines #1-#4 static PASS with bindings CURRENT incl. machine #4 source-arm64-sha256 re-bound, unpack 610/610). Published main == exo == 5d36b9dd, no force; fresh clone from GitHub verified (tip, hashes, build, make test ALL TESTS PASSED, static hello runs with 23 IRELATIVE). Receipts on the landed tree: make test ALL TESTS PASSED (tests2/153 runs natively), conformance 328/333 standing five, static gate cells green, TLS GD spot cells exact, arm64 encoding proof fixed word 0x8b3e63e0 x2 / buggy 0x8b1e03e0 x0 matching upstream HEAD. Cadence as ruled by Will 2026-11-08: wave-boundary checks only, NO cron. Next drift check at the D4 wave boundary. Process note: the first sync tree was destroyed mid-work when a ranchd-timed-out background git clone from GitHub failed and removed its target directory (which had been re-cloned locally at the same path); work was redone in a fresh directory (tree2) and no published state was affected — lesson: never reuse the target path of a timed-out clone.

