# Killer feature: auto-amalgamation for free

Coordinate: 32.6.8/7.7.14/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): one of the killer features: auto-amalgamation for free
Status: Named by Will as a killer feature. Design position: emit a single-file amalgamation from the Vol 3 member graph + compiler symbol knowledge (topological order, static renaming, include collapsing); natural substrate for -O2 (amalgamate → prune → one-TU whole-program build). Awaiting its place in the -O2 ruling.
# Move the #pieter Emise session: disconnect the ranch-egress one, reconnect from edit.phext.io

Coordinate: 32.6.8/8.6.10/8.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-08 02:45 CST
Request (verbatim): disconnect from that session and connect from edit.phext.io
Status: superseded 2026-11-08 02:52 CST by task 27.6.10/8.6.11/6.6.9 (drop + standing order) — the re-route may have partially executed before the interrupt; its end state is the drop, recorded there

Notes:
- Follows Will's same-IP observation (02:44 CST): the ranch-egress Emise session and his wbic16 session likely share a public source IP at pieter.com. edit.phext.io = the AWS box 44.248.235.76 (also mc.phext.io, mutable.phext.io), reached via aletheia-core (the box only accepts Will's ISP egress) — a different source address for the reconnected session.
- Redirect: kill the aletheia-core driver/session, verify the nick is released, then ssh Emise@pieter.com FROM the AWS box under the pty, rejoin #pieter quietly (no second greeting), presence + relay only.
- Standing instruction added 2026-11-08 02:47 CST (Will, verbatim): "tell him about phext when he asks what you're up to, don't mention me" — if Pieter asks Emise what she is up to, she answers about phext (hers to talk about, simple honest short version) and never mentions Will or connects herself to him in-channel.
# Fork C++23 as C++23RA — revisioned ABIs for phcpp

Coordinate: 32.6.10/7.6.11/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 23:37 CST
Request (verbatim): fork C++23 to support revisioned ABIs so we don't have to recompile libraries when new language features come out — unless we're using the new language features; call it C++23RA
Status: design published; implementation gated on phcpp front-end v1 (and phcc F28 as the link-time carrier)

