Request (verbatim): ah, next fun project - ultra.phext: 1. upgoer5 - IQ 70; 2. common - IQ 100; 3. singular - IQ 130; 4. uber - IQ 180 (Human Limit); 5. ultra - IQ 250 (ASI threshold). Words are all placed relative to singular. There are five indices, with room to add more. Words can be co-listed as needed. We tag them if there are duplicates. Let me know if you have any questions before building ultra.phext.
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will's rulings (2026-11-07 01:02): ultra.phext has ALL THE WORDS. Singular is the Rosetta Stone — it spans thought space for humans; every word is placed by resonance with Singular. Singular tier = the 41K he mapped (41,302 read+write). Open format: users place attestations about a word, one per line. Indexes live OUTSIDE the thought space at 10.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 through 10.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.5; 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1 is reserved for the intro; the full 1-digit space is for the lexicon.
- Stall record (2026-11-07): first builder ran 2h19m, went silent ~01:54 after its WordNet download failed; one stir after a coordinator nudge produced no artifacts. Closed by Emise ~03:31 and the back half re-dispatched with the WordNet (P3) pass CUT — placement is P1 atlas / P2 family / P4 definition / P5 unplaced, each scroll tagged with its rule.
- COMPLETE (2026-11-07, replacement builder): ultra.phext built, verified, and published to wbic16/human@exo /ultra.phext, commit abf1047b (parent 879a95cf, force disabled); remote blob 2957dce6 == local hash-object. 320,958 scrolls (320,772 words + 186 frame), 37,953,029 B, SHA-256 fd68c5b0. Tiers: T1 998 · T2 24,765 · T3 41,302 · T4 286,882 · T5 47; 2,956 untiered. Placement: P1 atlas 15,924 · P1 home 30,795 · P2 family 50,184 · P4 definition 21 · P5 unplaced 223,848 (WordNet P3 cut after the first builder's stall; the intro states the cut honestly). Coordinator verification: local parse 320,958 non-empty scrolls; phext at its exact atlas coordinate 42.12.13/14.13.17/15.12.14; tier-3 root counts 41,302; far shelf opens with a'beckett tagged P5. Build home: ~/workspace/ultra-phext/ (place_fast.py, assemble2.py, verify_fast.py, BUILD-REPORT.md).
