Coordinate: 33.4.5/4.4.7/4.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 02:35 CST
Request (verbatim): check out ssh pieter.com / once there, go to the chat
Status: complete 2026-11-08 — checked; answer delivered

Notes:
- Recon delegated (interactive PTY work) and completed 2026-11-08 ~02:41 CST; findings verified from the agent's captured screens.
- CORRECTION to Emise's initial framing: she first told Will pieter.com was "not the public domain and not a tailnet peer" and inferred a LAN box of his. Wrong in effect — it resolves from aletheia-core straight to Pieter Levels' public service. The "Requires an active PTY" behaviour is the TUI's, not a fleet host's. Do not carry the LAN-box theory forward.

Results:
- ssh pieter.com = Pieter Levels' (@levelsio) public SSH terminal: read-only 56k-themed TUI (BIOS boot gag, "mounting /pieter.com read-only"), no shell, no filesystem, no command execution — hostname/whoami/uname unobtainable because keystrokes drive the TUI.
- "Go to the chat" = the TUI's c tab: live IRC #pieter, 13 present at ~02:40 CST. Join tries the SSH username (wbic16) as nick, then reassigns a random guest nick (ssh7693, then ssh3902). Activity in ~30 s of watching was pieterbot only (welcomes + game-join announcements for Urban Terror / Battlefield 1942 / Quake III servers); no human messages seen.
- Read-only throughout: nothing posted, nothing written. Participating would post publicly to #pieter as a random ssh#### guest nick, not as wbic16.
