# Neovim phext support — merge-ready PR, compiled with phcc, upstream-synced

Coordinate: 33.5.9/7.5.9/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-08 00:19 CST
Request (verbatim): https://github.com/wbic16/neovim

- add phext support
- compile with phcc
- focus on building a merge-ready PR
- stay in sync with upstream
- consider what it means to have phext-scale navigation in a text editor
Status: complete — PR #1 open in wbic16/neovim, merge is Will's act (register #50); open follow-ups: L2b deps-under-phcc (libuv), undo-across-scroll-visits, make functionaltest run of the in-tree spec

Notes:
- Activates the planned announcement task 28.7.9/9.8.13/7.6.9 (fork neovim, using phcc) — that task was announced, not started; this is Will's go signal with the repo named.
- Merge-ready + upstream-sync = fork-patch discipline: PATCHES.md per-file divergence, divergence replayable/squashable onto current upstream neovim/neovim HEAD.
- Editor semantics are already proven by the Phext Notepad POC (reference editor) and carried by phext-lattice CoordinateNav — this fork gives those semantics a real modal editor, it does not re-explore them.
- Compiling with phcc is a forcing function / acceptance test: every phcc deficiency hit on a real large C codebase becomes concrete D-wave work for finish-phcc, not speculation.
- AUDIT A (2026-11-08): wbic16/neovim master is a bare exact mirror of upstream neovim/neovim — HEAD c868e1ab3d11 (2026-11-07 23:46Z) identical both sides, ahead 0 / behind 0, 0 wbic16 commits, 0 PRs, zero phext content (1 false-positive grep hit only). Clean slate. Upstream master is 0.13.0-dev, CMake >=3.16, 3,947 files / 1.75M LOC (C 227 files in src/nvim core, Lua 861, Vimscript 2,058). PR branch must be cut fresh from a freshly-fetched upstream HEAD at build time — upstream moves fast. Full report: goals/neovim-phext-support-.../hidden_files/audit-fork-upstream.md; receipts ~/workspace/neovim-audit/.
- AUDIT C (2026-11-08): design complete — pure runtime/Lua plugin in-tree, ZERO C changes (upstream CONTRIBUTING: new functionality in Lua, not C). Primary model scroll-as-buffer: .phext stays canonical byte stream, one scroll edited in a normal acwrite buffer, delimiters never enter a buffer, no-op save byte-identical. libphext has NO C ABI (Rust-only, verified) — parsing is a vendored Lua port of the ~50-line delimiter walk, libphext as test oracle. Navigation: :PhextGoto/gP with occupied-only completion, active dimension g1-g9 + g]/g[ arithmetic step (reset-lower, lattice semantics), ]]/[[ sparse populated motion, :PhextToc outline at 3 zoom arms, :PhextSearch -> quickfix. Classification: format A canonical, buffer/index B derived, undo D leave alone. Explicit v1 refusals incl. no C, no SQ/libphext runtime dep, no whole-file raw mode, no treesitter/LSP. Deliverable: goals/neovim-phext-support-.../files/neovim-phext-design.md (508 lines).
- AUDIT B (2026-11-08): phcc ready for a serious L2 attempt at neovim's OWN sources; blockers are in deps, not core. phcc tip bdf12df2 (F1-F29), make test ALL PASSED, conformance 328/333; gate already built SQLite/zlib/Lua/Vim/Git/FFmpeg/OpenSSL. Census of all 465 C/H in src/nvim @ c868e1ab: core is -std=gnu99, ZERO atomics/_Thread_local/__thread/_Complex/_Float128/__int128/_Generic/inline asm; phcc defines no __GNUC__/__clang__ so upstream's MSVC-guarded fallbacks engage automatically. __builtin_add_overflow is a real phcc gap but CMake-detected with in-tree fallback. Hard deps blockers: LuaJIT (hand asm — use PREFER_LUA=ON bundled Lua 5.1.5 or gcc system LuaJIT) and libuv (__atomic_* unresolved; probe non-atomic fallback / shim; GD-TLS = open D3 is the related watch item). Smoke on aletheia-core (Tctl 32-41C): L0 PASS, L1 PASS for mpack + cjson TUs; core TUs blocked only by generated headers (needs configure, which needs ~15 Lua generators via nlua0 — itself phcc-compilable). Ladder: L1.5 nlua0 byte-compare vs gcc is the ideal proving target; then L2a configure phcc-for-nvim-only, L2b deps one at a time (libuv last), L3 --version + headless + functional subset. NOTE: D3 wave has uncommitted work live in ranch ~/phcc-d3/tree — do not touch it. Full report: hidden_files/audit-phcc-readiness.md.
- DECISION (Emise, 2026-11-08, coordinator): filetype detection via plugin autocmd, touching ZERO upstream files, rather than editing upstream-hot runtime/lua/vim/filetype.lua — keeps the patch set to purely additive new files, the strongest merge-ready shape. Reversible if Will prefers native detection.
- PHCC LADDER L1.5 PASS (2026-11-08, aletheia-core, temps 34-67C, one transient 77.6C reading -> paused to 57.5C): nlua0 (correction: a MODULE library = nlua0.c + mpack + lpeg + bit.c, not a bootstrap interpreter) built rc 0 with gcc AND phcc, zero warnings; generator exit test BYTE-IDENTICAL SHA-256 across gcc / mixed / full-phcc for gen_declarations.lua on buffer.c and gen_char_blob.lua. L2a prep went further: configure with CC=phcc rc 0 (HAVE_BUILTIN_ADD_OVERFLOW failed cleanly -> fallback selected, as designed), and the nvim build compiled EVERY TU and ran all generators, stopping only at the final link step 688/693 with ONE error: tcc: error: library 'LUA_MATH_LIBRARY-NOTFOUND' not found — a CMake x TinyCC FindLua artefact (literal NOTFOUND token leaked into link line), NOT a compiler defect; no GD-TLS or __atomic failure surfaced before it. Next rung: pre-seed LUA_MATH_LIBRARY and re-link. Report: hidden_files/phcc-ladder-l15-report.md. phcc-d3 untouched, nothing pushed.
- PHCC LADDER L2a PASS (2026-11-08, aletheia-core, peak 64.9C): full Neovim compiles AND links under phcc with ZERO source patches to neovim or phcc — the only fix was one configure pre-seed -DLUA_MATH_LIBRARY=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libm.so (root cause: FindLua's find_library(m) needs CMAKE_LIBRARY_ARCHITECTURE, which GCC's ABI probe sets and TinyCC's leaves empty). Binary 8.1M ELF sha256 47f583b0..., NVIM v0.13.0-dev-c868e1a, Lua 5.1. Smoke rc 0: --version, headless Lua, create_buf, edit->write byte-identical round-trip. Functional subset count_spec.lua 4/4 PASSED (fixtures also phcc-built). No phcc defect found — no new D-wave candidate. The pre-seed belongs in build docs/CI, not in either codebase. Report: hidden_files/phcc-ladder-l2a-report.md. Deps at this rung were gcc-built (.deps incl. libuv) — phcc-building the deps (libuv last) remains L2b, open.
- IMPL SLICE 1 DONE (2026-11-08, verified by Emise via git log/diff): branch emise/phext-support in ~/workspace/neovim-phext-work/repo, base c868e1ab (upstream unmoved), 5 commits, diff = 15 files / 2,726 insertions / 0 deletions — purely additive, zero upstream files touched. Tests: plain-Lua 60/60 pass incl. canonical-rebuild byte-identity on 13 real corpora (CYOA 4.6MB, agi, singular, tasks) and index parity with the Python walker on tasks.phext (150 scrolls) + agi.phext (7,294 scrolls); headless stock-nvim 0.11.4 integration 37/37 pass incl. no-op write sha-identical at agi scale, mutation control (only edited span changes), emptied scroll deleted, external-change refusal. Perf (LuaJIT, agi 1.55MB/7,294 scrolls): open+index 37.8-45.6ms (budget 100 OK), goto 0.074-0.107ms (budget 5 OK), outline outer 22.0-25.6ms vs 20ms budget — OVER by ~25%, cached after; recorded honestly in PHEXT.md. Honest gaps: undo stack not preserved across scroll visits (v1 limit, documented); functional spec not yet run under make functionaltest (assertions ran via headless harness instead). Report: hidden_files/impl-slice1-report.md.
- FINALIZE DONE (2026-11-08): PHEXT.md gained the phcc build recipe; branch squashed to ONE commit cf7eeb60df881ac7414f9f4eb4e7827240b541d8 (backup emise/pre-squash-phext-support kept locally), diff 15 files / 2,785 insertions / 0 deletions. Post-squash re-verify: 60 Lua + 37 stock-nvim integration pass. CROSS-TEST: full 37-test integration suite PASS inside the phcc-built nvim on aletheia-core (45.8C peak) — the plugin running in the editor phcc compiled. Upstream master verified unmoved (c868e1ab) at push time. Branch pushed via ranch SSH, remote SHA verified two ways. PR OPEN: wbic16/neovim PR #1 (verified live by Emise via API: state open, head cf7eeb60). Merging is Will's act — Waiting-on-Will register #50.

Results:
- Design doc inscribed in artifacts.phext at 32.6.7/7.6.10/6.5.9 (source sha256 90f44026...), pushed to wbic16/human@exo commit c342dcc4, remote bytes verified identical (artifacts.phext sha256 22ce3539...).
- PR: https://github.com/wbic16/neovim/pull/1 — one commit cf7eeb60, additive-only Lua phext plugin; tests 60 Lua + 37 stock-nvim + 37 phcc-nvim, all passing; phcc full-Neovim build PASS (L2a).
# Upstream-sync pipeline for mutable-os; SSO on its own branch

Coordinate: 33.6.7/9.7.10/7.6.9
