# wishnode.net user testing — UI/UX pass for IQ 85-100 users

Coordinate: 34.5.6/5.4.7/5.4.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:33 CST
Request (verbatim): run user testing - ensure UI/UX passes for IQ=85-100 users
Status: in progress — baseline persona FAIL on task 3 recorded; fixes steered into rework; objective audit running; retest pending rebuilt site

Notes:
- Method (honest label): simulated user testing — IQ-calibrated persona walkthroughs on the real live site via browser + objective metrics (reading grade level of copy, jargon inventory, click-path depth, form clarity). NOT human-subject testing; real-user testing (e.g. via Daniele's office context) remains Will's option.
- Audience fit: personas drawn from the site's real audience — NE local/state government staff (county clerk's office, board secretary, agency admin).
- Findings steered into the 34.6.6 rework as binding copy rules: nav + per-page 'Ask about a pilot' path; plain-English lead summary per page; jargon translated at first use; engineering metadata moved to a 'For technical staff' section; material statute facts surfaced on main pages; every page ends with a plain next step; footer = company, no GitHub. Retest = same persona tasks against the rebuilt site (acceptance). Objective-metrics lane (reading levels, click paths) still running.
- Acceptance bar now binding on the 34.6.6 rework (steered in): per-page FK <=8 + FRE >=60 measured and reported, Details box -> 'Good to know', performance numbers translated to office terms, who/what-next block without invented registration facts, descriptive link labels, mobile media queries. Retest after rework: persona walkthrough + metrics re-run.

Results:
- BASELINE persona walkthrough DONE (2026-11-07 22:33-22:35 CST, live site): county-clerk office-manager persona — Task 1 (find Minutes Publisher) PASS; Task 2 (explain what it does + law) PASS with jargon friction; Task 3 (how to ask about trying it) FAIL — no contact/demo/pricing/form path anywhere; both page buttons exit to GitHub; footer 'Phext, Inc.' link goes to Will's personal GitHub profile. 17 documented stuck points: hash-chained audit log, phext/plain-text data format, synthetic/Nebraska-flavoured, computed, publishable artifact/HTML snapshot/hash prefix, repository/RFP language, Component/Default port 8802/SSO metadata block, 25,000-population threshold hidden in statute sheet, working-days interpretation unexplained on main page.
- OBJECTIVE AUDIT DONE (2026-11-07 22:35 CST): live pages FK grade 9.6-13.8 (bar <=8) FAIL; Reading Ease 25.7-54.5 (bar >=60) FAIL; ~25 unexplained jargon terms FAIL; clicks to app descriptions 1 PASS, to security 1 PASS, heading hierarchy PASS, length/subheads PASS; pilot/contact path nonexistent FAIL; proof = 1 click off-site to raw GitHub markdown FAIL; homepage first body sentence grade 20.4; security page worst (FK 13.8, FRE 25.7). Full report: ~/workspace/your_files/wishnode-ux-audit-34.5.6.md (incl. plain-language rewrites of the 5 worst sentences).
