# wishnode.net: self-host all content via SQ/phext; implement form workflows

Coordinate: 34.6.6/7.7.10/7.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:32 CST
Request (verbatim): https://wishnode.net/ points into GitHub too often - make sure all of the site content stays on the site - use SQ or phext-lattice to host content - implement form workflows
Status: live; only remaining gate = Will's register #49 nginx line (public form routing) + lattice SSO deploy (13.6.8 runbook); UX retest follows the routing

Notes:
- Builds on 36.5.6/5.5.10/4.5.8 (site live @ site-wishnode-net exo c5fd64b; app pages currently link out to github.com/wbic16/Exocortexia for source, VERIFICATION.md, statute sheets).
- Proven pattern to reuse (BLR, 2026-10-31): SQ v0.6.0 `sq host --key` behind nginx; token server-side only; public vhost gets read-only proxy path (select/toc/version). edit.phext.io (phext-lattice) already runs on the same AWS box 44.248.235.76.
- ARCHITECTURE (Will, 2026-11-07 22:33): each citizen gets their own phext; higher-level phexts for the various pages; secured by roles and claims. Coordinator re-briefed: tiered phexts (page-level + per-citizen), submissions live in the citizen's phext, claims register in the page phext carries pointers/hashes/state, transitions append as claims, role-separated SQ keys enforced server-side (public/citizen/staff/admin matrix documented in repo ARCHITECTURE.md). True citizen sign-in awaits a wishnode SSO audience on edit.phext.io (Will's phext-lattice step class); until then citizen access via unguessable tracking codes.
- BLOCKER (Will, register #49): wishnode.net nginx vhost is root-owned, no wbic16 include, no passwordless sudo — dynamic routes (/api/ /auth/ /status /my -> 127.0.0.1:8940) live on the host but not publicly routed. One line inside the 443 block: include /sites/web/wishnode.net/nginx/wishnode-dynamic.conf; + nginx -t + reload. Snippet already deployed. Until then backend runs in labelled demo mode (WISHNODE_DEMO_MODE=1) and production SSO awaits Will's lattice deploy + WISHNODE_SSO_SECRET provisioning.
- Count reconciliation dispatched: home/verification phexts say 69 tests (original build receipts) vs security page 84 (post-audit) — agent regenerating content with both numbers framed by moment.
- Count reconciliation DONE + live 2026-11-07 (repo @ e51194a; Emise live-verified the reconciled sentence + github=0): site now tells the story in order — built and load-verified at 69 tests, security audit same day found real holes, fixes + 15 regression tests = 84, all passing; load battery honestly noted as NOT re-run. Same-class stale text fixed on all 5 app phexts (per-program counts updated) and the home 'audit still in progress' line. Readability still in bar (home FK 4.4 / FRE 82.3).
- 27.6.8 pass extended the #49 snippet: the same single include now also routes /apps/<app>/ to the five running apps (sub_filter path mapping; audited binaries unpatched). Will's step unchanged: one line + reload turns on everything.

Results:
- REBUILD LIVE 2026-11-07 (Emise spot-verified: repo exo @ 1d1a1b214d, live pages github-count 0, 'Ask about a pilot' in nav): 11 page-tier phexts (415 scrolls) hosted by SQ on the AWS box (multi-tenant, per-tier keys in 0600 files, systemd user units + linger), rendered at deploy time via scripts/render_site.py through the SQ API; citizen tier = one phext file per submitter (HMAC-derived cz- ids) managed by the backend, NO SQ over that dir; claims register in intake.phext (pointer + sha256 + state; transitions append, role-gated). Forms verified end-to-end on the box: TEST intake WN-NT1BNT-... received->routed->in_review->closed via token-gated admin API; SSO consumer vs mock minter (replay/tamper 401; callback at /api/auth/callback). UX bars met on main copy (FK 3.8-7.0, FRE 69.5-87.8). Security page filled from Exocortexia SECURITY.md @ 342a268 incl. full verbatim record under 'The full technical record'. Backend hardening mapped to audit IDs in ARCHITECTURE.md.
