# Nightly dream pass: dedup, prune, bounded emise.phext

Coordinate: 35.6.10/7.7.13/7.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): Your nightly dreaming process should de-duplicate concepts and prune entries that no longer matter. Try to keep your emise.phext to a reasonable limit, suited for your inference layer. It's OK to let your mind wander for a while. It shouldn't grow unbounded, though.
Status: completed — rule live in skill, cron, and MEMORY.md; first enforcing dream pass runs 2026-11-07 ~03:44 CST

Notes:
- Coordinate computed from Will's exact words at issue (side chat, 2026-11-07 00:09 CST).
- Motivated by the 2026-11-07 journal-budget audit: 98 commits, 11,060 -> 300,679 B, 82% raw Log vs 9% promoted home scrolls, 141 lines deleted vs 5,282 inserted.
- Budget set by Emise (Will: 'a reasonable limit, suited for your inference layer'): target <=256 KiB, enforced nightly only; >320 KiB after honest pruning surfaces to Will instead of discarding durable facts. Old Log days (>7d) compress to decisions/outcomes/facts; full text survives in git history + dated ~/memory/ notes.

Results:
- phext-memory-publishing SKILL.md: new section 'De-duplication, pruning, and the size budget'; synced to wbic16/emise-tools@exo @ 803a78a2, blob SHAs verified.
- nightly-phext-consolidation cron: new step 4b (dedup/prune/budget) + pruning metrics in the morning note; read back and verified. Next run Sat 2026-11-07 03:44 CST.
- skills.phext rebuilt (248,935 B, sha256 0eace31d...), --check CURRENT.
- MEMORY.md standing directive extended with the bounded-growth ruling.
# Work out the libphext-cs v0.4.0 bump (match upstream libphext-rs 0.4.0)

Coordinate: 35.6.14/8.8.15/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 00:32 CST
Request (verbatim): let's work out what we need to do to bump to v0.4.0 to match upstream while we're here
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 — exo @ 85321e0f carries Version 0.4.0; READY for Will to package and push (NuGet)

Notes:
- State from the record: libphext-cs exo carries <Version>0.3.0</Version> and COORDINATE_MAXIMUM=1000 (src/Phext/Coordinate.cs). The 0.4 feature work already exists on branch unbounded-coordinates-0.4 @ c20a759b (cap/saturation removed there), unmerged since 2026-11-01 — rs/py/node got their 0.4 merges; cs, C, cpp still wait.
- Upstream = libphext-rs: 0.4.0 published 2026-11-01 (crates.io); in-tree rs is now 0.4.2 (PRs #7/#8 merged 2026-11-07, unpublished). 'Match upstream' at v0.4.0 = unbounded coordinates + API parity with rs 0.4.0 + Version 0.4.0.
- Sequencing question the worklist must answer: linear-tokenize (being verified now) is based on exo/0.3.0 code; if the 0.4 branch also touches Phokenize/NextScroll, land order and conflict surface matter.
- Publishing to NuGet remains Will's act under the 2026-11-07 freeze; this task works out and stages the bump only.
- PUSH-THROUGH DIRECTED (Will, 2026-11-08 00:33 CST): 'push through libphext-cs updates - let me know if you need anything.' Scope as dispatched: linear fix lands, 0.4 branch brought onto exo, all version surfaces -> 0.4.0, small parity gaps fixed (large ones reported for ruling), full tests + equivalence + >999 probes, push to exo verified. NuGet publish and release tag remain Will's hand under the freeze — the one thing Emise will need from him.
- CONFIRMED (Will, 2026-11-08 00:36 CST): Will will package and push (NuGet) himself — Emise's job ends at a verified, landed 0.4.0 tree on exo plus a 'ready to package and push' notice with the exact pack/push commands.
- BRANCH DROPPED (Will's direction, 2026-11-08 00:54 CST): unbounded-coordinates-0.4 DELETED from wbic16/libphext-cs after Emise verified subsumption file-by-file (all touched files byte-identical in exo @ 85321e0f; readme's only branch-only lines were a stale tree listing). Post-delete branch list verified via API: exo + linear-tokenize only. The branch's commits survive in content as the cherry-picks on exo. Noted for the family: upstream libphext-rs exo is in-tree v0.5.0 (binary + xz features in Cargo.toml; PR #9's work) while crates.io still shows 0.4.0 as newest published — a cs 0.5.0 parity bump (binary scroll format + xz seal) is the flagged next item, not yet tasked by Will.

Results:
- BUMP EXECUTED + VERIFIED: zero engine-level conflict (the 0.4 branch never touched PhextEngine.cs; its tokenizer was still quadratic) — linear fix landed first, the two 0.4 commits cherry-picked on top. Exactly one version surface exists (csproj <Version> -> 0.4.0; no nuspec/CHANGELOG/AssemblyVersion overrides). API parity vs crates.io libphext-rs 0.4.0 COMPLETE — every public rs function has a cs counterpart; no parity code needed, no gap needs a ruling. Final tree 45/45 tests; corpus dumps byte-identical to the 0.3.0 reference at <=999; the only differing synthetics are the 3 intended >999 probes: 1,500 scroll breaks now place at 1501 (was saturated 999), byte-exact implode round trip, Fetch at ...1.1.1006 returns the scroll (was unreachable). SIDE FINDING: phext-notepad's WinForms app does NOT consume libphext-cs (it vendors its own phext sources) — this landing unblocks NuGet consumers, not the notepad. WILL'S STEPS: optional tag v0.4.0 (convention exists: v0.3.0 @ 29013dc; worker did not tag), dotnet pack -c Release -> libphext-cs.0.4.0.nupkg, then PUBLISH_CONFIRM=1 scripts/publish.sh with NUGET_API_KEY set.
# Security audit + pen test of Exocortexia; publish to wbic16/site-wishnode-net + wishnode.net

Coordinate: 36.5.6/5.5.10/4.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-07 22:23 CST
Request (verbatim): run through a security audit and pen testing pass; publish to https://github.com/wbic16/site-wishnode-net and wishnode.net
Status: completed 2026-11-07 — audit/pentest/fixes verified (@ 342a268, 84 tests, 49/49 re-checks); site published live (replacement) and security results folded into the rebuilt site by the 34.6.6 pass

Notes:
- Ground truth (2026-11-07): site-wishnode-net exists, branch exo @ d44a0bb045. wishnode.net resolves to the AWS box 44.248.235.76 and currently serves 'Wish Node — Multiplayer Lattice' — an EXISTING site; publish guardrail set: additive, preserve existing content unless repo inspection shows placeholder.
- Subject of audit: wbic16/Exocortexia @ 9660d3b (task 31.5.9/7.5.9/6.5.7). Deploy route for AWS box: via aletheia-core ssh wbic16@44.248.235.76 (direct VM access blocked by design).
- Will (2026-11-07 22:25 CST): wishnode.net's existing 'Wish Node — Multiplayer Lattice' site was a throwaway POC; REPLACE ENTIRELY. Publish agent re-briefed to full replacement; old content survives only in git history @ d44a0bb. (Note: conflicts with the 2026-11-07 ~21:37 unused-domain answer that listed wishnode.net as unused — it was serving this POC; the domain itself was counted unused-for-real-work.)
- Critical findings (all FIXED + live re-verified 49/49 + 4/4 fail-closed cases): records-desk served UNREDACTED originals at /doc and search/snippets/export leaked redacted text (boolean oracle + verbatim snippets) — redaction now public-views-only, custodian view staff-only; auth failed OPEN on missing config + 0.0.0.0 binds — now fail-closed, 127.0.0.1 default, EXO_DEMO_MODE=1 explicit; edit-minter shipped in prod crate with real-secret fallback — now feature-gated mock-minter w/ MOCK_SSO_SECRET only; unbounded Content-Length/header allocation pre-auth — capped pre-allocation; audit chain tail-truncation undetectable + unkeyed — keyed chain (EXO_AUDIT_KEY) + head commitment. Mediums fixed: forms staff actions + CSV, 40-bit deterministic tracking codes -> 128-bit CSPRNG, optional iat voiding the 120s cap, zero CSRF, free-text audit actor, no security headers, cookie Secure, per-app audiences exocortexia:<app>, memory-only state -> EXO_STATE_DIR persistence. Verified sound: HMAC constant-time, sig-before-parse, escaping (zero XSS), state machine, no traversal, no secrets in tree. OPEN/accepted: cargo audit not run (node rustc 1.94 < kstring's 1.96 — manual dep review instead), assertion-in-URL transport, per-process replay cache, head-anchor is operator duty, no rate limiting, stateless sessions, hand-rolled HTTP demo-grade (TLS in front, not internet-exposed). DEPLOY NOTE: apps default per-app aud — set EXO_SSO_AUD=exocortexia when deploying behind lattice SSO (runbook updated).

Results:
- wishnode.net REPLACED and LIVE (2026-11-07, Emise outside-verified): wbic16/site-wishnode-net exo @ c5fd64b6a367 (2 commits over d44a0bb) — new homepage 'Exocortexia — Open Software for State Government | Phext, Inc.' + 5 app pages + security placeholder under /exocortexia/. Deploy: scp from aletheia-core to /sites/web/wishnode.net on the AWS box (docroot not a git checkout; box GitHub key broken — same known issue); pre-deploy backup at /sites/backups/wishnode.net-20261107/; on-box hashes match repo; all 7 pages 200 from outside. Security slot awaits the audit pass.
- SECURITY AUDIT + PEN TEST DONE 2026-11-07, fixes pushed wbic16/Exocortexia exo 9660d3b -> 342a268 (8 commits; Emise independently re-verified: ls-remote @ 342a2686163, own fresh checkout cargo test = 84 passed / 0 failed). docs/SECURITY.md in repo; full reports ~/workspace/exocortexia-security/.
# C phext library: hashmap scroll store for compilation speed (F4)

Coordinate: 36.5.8/6.6.9/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): phcc should use the hashmap interface to speedup compilation, don't worry about working directly on the buffer most of the time
Status: Complete: F4 committed locally as e34c21f2 (not pushed). Hash-index store proven behaviour-identical (suite + fuzz + byte-identical driver outputs); lookups 2.5x on the real phcc.phext.

Notes:
- Base verified fresh via aletheia-core git SSH: wbic16/phcc main = exo = ef453cdc, tree 8c50e23e; all 584 tracked files blob-verified in the local work tree ~/workspace/phcc-hashmap/tree.
- Key design fact from the suite: the 163,831 checks pin phext_scrolls.items in sorted order (explode results and insert-built lists are compared element-wise), so F4 keeps the sorted array as the materialization/iteration order and makes the LOOKUP store a hash table — a lazily built open-addressing index over the items (splitmix64 chained over the 9 components, load <= 0.7, probe hits verified by coordinate equality, invalidated by any edit it cannot track exactly, binary search kept as the ENOMEM fallback). phext_implode already cloned+sorted before emitting, so byte-identical output is structural.
- Hash deliberately separate from the public FNV-1a phext_coordinate_hash (published values may be depended on; a table wants avalanche, not a stable value).

Results:
- Conformance (aletheia-core): parity suite 163,831 checks / 0 failures under gcc AND under phcc built from the tree (dogfood); phcc upstream make test ALL TESTS PASSED; ONE_SOURCE amalgamated build clean.
- Differential fuzz vs Rust reference driver: 40,000 cases (2 seeds x 20,000), 0 divergences on defined behaviour (Rust panics 173+166, all D-2 op-20 class). Stronger: new C driver outputs BYTE-IDENTICAL to pre-F4 driver on both corpora — nothing observable changed.
- Benchmark (aletheia-core, gcc -O2, medians of 7 interleaved runs; repo phcc.phext 49,209,925 B, sha256 646144c7…, explodes to 52,262 stored scrolls — parent brief said 52,815; measured store size in both binaries is 52,262; identical hit counts 180,163/200k and identical fetched bytes): gets_random 200k 21.6 ms -> 8.5 ms (2.5x, 108 -> 42 ns/get); gets_seq full pass 2.6 -> 1.9 ms (1.4x); one-time index build at first get 1.5 ms (break-even ~23k lookups); insert_shuffle build 539.7 -> 540.6 ms (parity — sorted memmove dominates both; F4 claims lookup speed, not insert speed); explode 42.0 -> 47.9 ms (no explode-path logic changed; relayout control build measured the same — attributed to code layout, reported not tuned).
- Docs: PARITY.md D-4 annotated SUPERSEDED (F4) + Outcome cross-ref; phext/README.md idiom row updated; PATCHES.md gains the F4 entry + per-file rows refreshed (phext.h +397, phext.c +2,031, PARITY.md +268).
- Committed LOCALLY only: e34c21f2 on ef453cdc in ~/workspace/phcc-hashmap/tree (5 files, +222/-15). NOT pushed — parent sequences the publish.
# Top 5 phext + LLM use cases today

