# Study learn.h5i.dev (MiniLean4) in depth

Coordinate: 38.5.7/7.6.10/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-06 22:56 CST
Request (verbatim): https://learn.h5i.dev/ - study this in-depth!
Status: complete — full study delivered 2026-11-06

Notes:
- Site identified 2026-11-06: 'MiniLean4 — Implementing an Interactive Theorem Prover from Scratch' by Hideaki Takahashi (h5i-dev). A free online book building a Lean 4-style proof kernel in Rust (<3000 lines claimed), with the kernel running live in-browser (Wasm). 14 chapters + appendices A–F + bibliography; EN/JA/ZH. Repo: github.com/h5i-dev/MiniLean4.
- Study: ~/workspace/h5i-study/STUDY.md (all 20 pages read; repo cloned, built, tests run live: 25/25 pass). Book's claims verified: kernel 1,398 lines (claim <1,500); implementation 2,219 lines excl. tests, zero Cargo dependencies (claim <3,000, no deps); positivity.rs exactly 80 lines as claimed; reduction fuel 20,000 exact; Apache-2.0; repo created 2026-10-24, 79 commits, active. Accuracy: universe design is genuinely Lean's (Sort u : Sort u+1, imax, one impredicative bottom); consistency proof sound for the CORE system only, with strong normalization imported from literature — book says so itself; inductives deferred to Werner 1994 CIC. Relevance: template for a small trusted checker in SQ's orbit + Ch.4 method for machine-checking SBOR consistency; NOT a usable proof assistant (no unification/implicits, proofs discarded at qed).
