# Play-test the Roads games at 6, 8, and 10 year old reference points; iterate and improve

Coordinate: 38.6.7/9.5.11/5.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): do some play-testing at 6, 8, and 10 year old reference points - iterate and improve
Status: Complete: tested at 6/8/10 reference points, fixes built and published to the repo (45997404, tree-verified).

Notes:
- Method: rubric-based reference-point testing (no real children available) — one tester pass per age against explicit reading/number/motor/attention profiles, auditing the shipped game files (~/workspace/roads-to-the-future/publish/*.html) plus simulating play sequences from the game logic; findings must cite evidence (UI text, target sizes, number ranges, line lengths).
- Fixes ship as artifact edits, then re-export + re-push to wbic16/site-apertureshift-com@exo, tree-verified.

Results:
- Three reference-point reports written (~/workspace/roads-to-the-future/playtest-age6.md, -age8.md, -age10.md): rubric-based simulation (source audits, Monte-Carlo replicas of Word Home's perturb() at 4,000 and 20,000 trials), limits stated in each.
- Findings that drove the redesign: Word Home was a BLOCKER at all three ages (guessing ~3.3/10 at 6/8; at 10 the medoid/consensus exploit scored 83-88% and Duel's fixed order rigged Red ~3.1 vs Blue ~1.9); Nine Numbers ran 393 taps with hold-overshoot star loss; Zap's full-word hint voided its star economy and cascade-unplace could delete a Duet partner's tiles.
- Fixes shipped per game as three paths (Little/Standard/Master): Word Home evidence-on-screen (9 bars per address, neighbor addresses shown, landmark cast, specials as tutorial rounds 1-2 in every game incl. Duel with alternating assignment, Master distractors = real coordinates, assisted-marking, grey miss nodes); Nine Numbers hold auto-stop at target, pars 3..64 (238 taps), Little Road (digits <=5), Express Road ({1,5} coin-opt par, timers), Race board framing, on-device persistence; Zap read-then-build cards, Little Lines (no star costs), single-tile undo, hint priced at -1 star, Encore (no length dots, global distractors, badges).
- Published: commit 45997404 on wbic16/site-apertureshift-com@exo (parent 01d03a30), remote tree blob-verified against local publish tree — all 10 files match, no extras.
- Still owed: live in-browser playthrough of the new modes; live apertureshift.com flip (domain does not deploy from this repo).
# Notepad++ phext support: free-form subspace views + libphext-cpp parity at 0.5.0

Coordinate: 38.6.8/8.7.12/6.6.12
Issued: 2026-11-08 01:02 CST
Request (verbatim): Notepad++ Support

Resume the patch to Notepad++ for phext support - we want free-form subspace views in Notepad++ - not per-scroll interfacing. We probably need to get the C++ fork of libphext up to parity with libphext-rs v0.5.0

https://github.com/wbic16/notepad-plus-plus

1. review the partial patches
2. update to follow latest
3. finish patching phext-native support for notepad-plus-plus
Status: phase 1 complete + pushed + Actions-green 2026-11-08 — remaining: Will merges branches; phase-2 UI + library swap are follow-ons

Notes:
- Design constraint (Will, 2026-11-08): free-form subspace views in Notepad++, NOT per-scroll interfacing. Subspace = a contiguous/selected region of the 9D space rendered/edited as a document, rather than one editor buffer per scroll.
- SUBSPACE DESIGN LANDED (2026-11-08): ~/workspace/notepadpp-phext/SUBSPACE-DESIGN.md, 789 lines, sha256 9963471ddd5bf78f0ed2e2b8327eda792d9fd1268979ebf30a7ab4496b1d596e (Emise hash-verified). Key findings: fork tip 549d7a0 'Partial up-dimension navigation' 2023-11-24 (~upstream 8.5/8.6 era) vs upstream 8.9.8.1 (Sep 2026, Scintilla 5.6.6) — plan is rebase-first / new feature on 8.9.x informed by the 2023 attempt, not finishing a nearly-done patch. Plugin API proven insufficient for the data path (notifications only, no byte-stream ownership) — load/save + phext buffer type are core-patch-only; Navigator/dialogs/menus are plugin-carryable. Design: 9D Fixed/Range/Free subspace spec, 6 presets (whole volume, one chapter, 3D slice, scroll line, strided, whole file), separator lines editable-as-structure with blocked-save-on-corruption (never silent guess), splice save rule (verbatim bytes outside edited regions, no-edit open/save = SHA-256 identical), sparse offset index (populated scrolls only). 8 open questions each with a recommended default in §6.
- LIBPHEXT-CPP PARITY AUDIT LANDED (2026-11-08): ~/workspace/libphext-cpp-parity/PARITY.md, 519 lines, sha256 b8262dd989be11c6cd5a99030da9c272ee6deebd478582ab3fc7e82a2f9ab8bf (Emise hash-verified). HEADs: cpp master 1153714c2f, cpp unbounded-coordinates-0.4 dd1578b1e9 (delta vs master: uint16->uint32 Coordinate + scripts only), rs exo e85d8b5676 (0.5.0). RS tests re-run: 78 passed all-features / 63 default, after supplying gitignored unit-test.phext fixture (clean RS clone cannot build its own seal tests). SCORE: 44 capabilities — 1 present, 9 partial, 4 divergent, 30 missing. CPP has NO per-coordinate API at all (no fetch/insert/replace/remove, no explode/implode, no coordinate parse/validate); it is a load/dump/nav-tree container (trs::string). Master has a disguised cap: uint16 fields wrap 65535->0 (probe-verified, 0 becomes a live map key); unbounded branch wraps at 2^32; RS is uncapped usize. Binary scrolls + xz seal + XXH3-128 checksum + manifest entirely missing in CPP. Silent-corruption divergences: Break::LINE=0x10 not 0x0A, loadTerse does not reset state, getSummaryText 64-byte cap without ellipsis. PORT PLAN P0-P9 (~2-3 engineer-weeks, test-porting dominated): conformance harness first (vendor unit-test.phext), coordinate core, subspace core, phokenize/explode/implode, index/offset, checksum (vendored xxHash single-header), binary (hand-rolled strict base64, no dep), xz via optional liblzma off-by-default mirroring RS feature flag. Recommendation: new header-only phext.h free-function API mirroring RS, trs::string kept as legacy wrapper, base on unbounded branch.
- PATCH REVIEW LANDED (2026-11-08): ~/workspace/notepadpp-phext/REVIEW.md, sha256 6bb1c553d8499651498ef1ae8affe52a0bd78e656ac4b2cdaf386193ebeb5ece (Emise hash-verified); evidence: full-diff.patch (4,907 lines) + 25 per-file diffs alongside. Fork base: upstream 2768cf54, 2 commits past v8.6 (N++ 8.6 / Scintilla 5.3.8, Nov 2023). Divergence: 8 phext commits, 30 files, +3044/-578. ARCHITECTURE OF 2023 PATCH: Scintilla Document's single CellBuffer replaced by a 9-deep MappedDimension tree of per-scroll CellBuffers (one buffer per scroll — exactly the model Will ruled out), 31 hand-added messages 6000-6030 in autogenerated headers (Scintilla.iface untouched, regeneration wipes them), Enter hijacked to jump-to-next-scroll, vendored headers duplicated in PowerEditor/src/phext and scintilla/src/phext and already diverged from each other; NOT libphext in any version. DOES NOT COMPILE/RUN AS SHIPPED: only Debug|x64 bumped to C++20 (headers use std::map::contains); resource.h shifts menu indices but Notepad_plus.rc never got a Phext popup (items land in Encoding menu, all submenu fetches off by one); loadFileData truncates EVERY file >128KiB on load; phext tree never cleared so deleted scrolls resurrect on save; phextIncrement computes a request it never sends (navigation reloads the file, modal prompt per step when dirty); isPhextEnabled always true (coordinate readout on plain text too); no .phext registration — detection sniffs bytes 0x01/0x17-0x1F in first block. Upstream now d87f8bd8 (2026-11-07), 1,648 commits past base, v8.9.9 / Scintilla 5.6.9; mitigations: CellBuffer seam and message block 6000-6030 still unclaimed upstream, loadFileData signature unchanged; upstream switched TCHAR->wchar_t in Buffer API.
- BUILD PHASE 1 DISPATCHED (2026-11-08): (A) libphext-cpp parity port per PARITY.md P0-P9 — new header-only phext.h mirroring RS 0.5.0 incl binary+xz, conformance tests ported from RS, branch emise/parity-0.5.0 based on unbounded branch, local commits only, coordinator pushes. (B) Notepad++ build on upstream d87f8bd8 branch emise/phext-subspace — 2023 Document surgery DISCARDED; model beside Scintilla (PhextDocument + Projection, standalone-tested in C++17), minimal core wiring (.phext registration, real Phext menu, load/save bypass), PATCHES.md + PHEXT.md, local commits only. MSVC/Windows build verification is a known gap this phase (no MSVC on this box).
- NOTEPAD++ PHASE 1 LANDED (2026-11-08): ~/workspace/notepadpp-phext/build/, branch emise/phext-subspace @ 1bb22459dbd7 (base upstream d87f8bd8 v8.9.9+2, 3 staged commits, NOT pushed; old fork master untouched; zero Scintilla/Lexilla files modified). Core (PowerEditor/src/phext/, single canonical copy, C++17): phext_core.h (unbounded Coordinate + canonical append_scroll mirroring RS 0.5.0; documented libphext-cpp swap-in point), PhextDocument (sparse offset index, populated scrolls only), SubspaceSpec (Fixed/Range/Free, presets P0-P5), Projection (separator lines editable-as-structure, bidirectional offset map, corrupted separator = blocked save, splice write-back verbatim outside region, no-edit = byte-identical; strided views: text scatter OK, structural edits refused loudly). EMISE INDEPENDENT RE-RUN: run_tests.sh synthetic 100 passed 0 failed; with CYOA+Incipit+emise+agi corpora 136 passed 0 failed, ALL FOUR byte-identical round-trips (incl forced-canonical splice, mapping-equal=1); agi 1.47MB/7281 populated: load 49ms, project 194ms, splice 401ms on this VM. NOTE: BUILD-REPORT claims 201 checks; my runner count is 136 for the same corpora — counting difference unresolved (likely glue/extra runs), pass/fail and byte-identity both hold. WIRING (Windows-only, code-complete, NOT MSVC-compiled): extension-only .phext detection (no sniffing; .phext.xz refused with message), byte-faithful load/save via model bypassing encoding/EOL, Buffer::isPhext (no always-true bug), &Phext popup appended LAST (MENUINDEX_PHEXT 15, no existing index shifts), IDM_PHEXT at IDM+9500, status-bar coordinate from projection map, File Info + Repair Separators handlers functional, dialog commands stubbed TODO PHEXT-PHASE2. PATCHES.md + PHEXT.md in repo root. Remaining: MSVC compile/fix + smoke test (Windows access options put to Will 2026-11-08: GitHub Actions and/or OpenSSH-over-Tailscale script), phase-2 UI (Open Subspace dialog, Navigator, session spec persistence).
- LIBPHEXT-CPP PORT LANDED (2026-11-08): ~/workspace/libphext-cpp-build/clone, branch emise/parity-0.5.0 @ 22191c2e7c (base unbounded dd1578b1e9, 3 commits, NOT pushed). New header-only phext.h (sha256 767d017e5da372c39f13e76596c8832d672864f3904c63172510eb3d9fbcd089, Emise hash-verified) mirroring RS 0.5.0 function-for-function incl quirks; uint64_t coords no cap; vendored xxHash 0.8.3 single-header for XXH3-128; hand-rolled strict base64; xz behind PHEXT_CPP_WITH_XZ + liblzma, off by default. SCORE: 44/44 present (was 1/44). Tests: 82 tests, 163,897 checks, 0 failures; differential vs the real RS crate: 15,446 comparisons, 0 mismatches; seals BYTE-IDENTICAL to RS on 308/308 docs. unit-test.phext vendored into tests/ (sha256 4c101678..., matches audit fixture). xz-enabled build verified with xz 5.4.5 tarball headers (5 tests/21 checks) since this box lacks liblzma-dev. EMISE INDEPENDENT RE-RUN of scripts/test.sh: ALL TESTS PASS (seal SKIP in default config, as designed). Report: ~/workspace/libphext-cpp-build/BUILD-REPORT.md.
- WINDOWS ACCESS DECISION (Will, 2026-11-08 01:50 CST): 'Just GitHub Actions for now' — MSVC verification via windows-latest runners; the OpenSSH-over-Tailscale script (~/workspace/notepadpp-phext/setup-windows-ssh.ps1) is prepared but NOT to be used unless Will revisits. Actions worker dispatched: add phext-build.yml (core-msvc + app-x64-release) to emise/phext-subspace and msvc.yml to emise/parity-0.5.0, push both branches via aletheia-core SSH route (no force), watch runs, fix MSVC fallout in the wiring until green or genuinely blocked.
- ACTIONS PHASE LANDED + EMISE API-VERIFIED (2026-11-08): both branches pushed via bundle->aletheia-core->SSH, no force, hashes verified both ends. wbic16/notepad-plus-plus emise/phext-subspace @ 402a37621e8b; wbic16/libphext-cpp emise/parity-0.5.0 @ d1cc463f7c64 (Emise re-read both branch heads via GitHub API). Runs (Emise re-read conclusions via API): phext-build 42462513355 SUCCESS, upstream CI_build 42462513384 SUCCESS (all 13 jobs: MSVC x6 configs, CMake, MinGW/UCRT/Clang), libphext-cpp 42461233125 SUCCESS. MSVC fallout fixed (3): (1) cpp test_phokenize.cpp missing <algorithm> (phext.h itself compiled clean under cl first try); (2) REAL WIRING BUG — phase-1 save-splice block sat in backupCurrentBuffer() while saveBuffer() had NO phext branch (phext saves would have hit the encoding/EOL convertor and corrupted break bytes); moved into saveBuffer fail-closed + backup got its own splice branch; CRLF preserved (first edit's LF flip caught pre-push, redone, diff +110/-36); (3) CMake LNK2001 — core .cpps registered in CMakeLists next to Buffer.cpp. Library swap (phext_core.h -> libphext-cpp phext.h) deliberately NOT done: not a drop-in (dimension-indexed array core vs RS string-level API; both define phext::Coordinate) — a design task, semantics already agree, core re-verified 118 passed incl agi byte-identical on final tree. Report: ~/workspace/notepadpp-phext/ACTIONS-REPORT.md. REMAINING (Will-gated / follow-on): merge both branches (Will's act), phase-2 UI (Open Subspace dialog, Navigator, session spec persistence), library-swap design task, human GUI smoke test on Windows (Actions proves build + core, not interactive use).

Results:
- wbic16/notepad-plus-plus @ emise/phext-subspace 402a37621 — phext-build + upstream CI_build (13 jobs) SUCCESS on windows-latest
- wbic16/libphext-cpp @ emise/parity-0.5.0 d1cc463f7 — 44/44 parity at RS 0.5.0, Actions SUCCESS (MSVC + ubuntu incl xz seal suite)
# Roads to the Future: games for every age group up to 20

Coordinate: 38.14.19/16.15.19/15.14.18
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): Consider games we need for every age group up to 20
Status: Considered and documented; awaiting Will's pick of the next band to build.

Notes:
- Full ladder written to ~/workspace/roads-to-the-future/AGES-0-20.md.
- Frame: the brick ratio is the age dial — all-Duplo at 0-2, Duplo-led 3-5, 30/60/10 at 6-9, Lego-led/K'Nex-rising 10-12, K'Nex-led 13-15, mechanism 16-17, raw phext 18-20.
- Built so far covers 6-12 (3 games x Little/Standard/Master paths). New designs: 0-2 Tap Home + Listen Mode; 3-5 Sort the Scrolls, One Number Road, Echo Tiles; 10-12 Scroll Seeker + Place a Word; 13-15 Kardashev Climb + Find It Fast + Exocortex Quest I; 16-17 Neuralese + The Long Road (CYOA); 18-20 Your Own Archive (Explorer productized), Runway sim, The Choir capstone.
- Proposed build order by adjacency: 3-5 first, then the two 10-12 games, then 13-15, 16-17, 18-20 hand-off last.
# Phext Notepad: sync scrolls directly with edit.phext.io

Coordinate: 39.4.7/7.4.9/5.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 00:57 CST
Request (verbatim): also, update phext notepad to directly interact with edit.phext.io for syncing scrolls
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 — branch emise/edit-sync @ a9f604e7 pushed; OAuth paste-step deviation + desktop-assertion follow-up await Will

Notes:
- Goal: phext-notepad connects to edit.phext.io (phext-edit, phext-lattice) and syncs at SCROLL granularity — fetch/push individual scrolls by coordinate against the server library — not whole-file upload (edit has no upload and no per-user space; library is server-side, gated by OAuth sign-in + approved-editors list, per lattice source read 2026-11-02; worker re-reads current source).
- Crux unknowns the worker resolves from the lattice source first: phext-edit's actual HTTP routes for scroll get/insert/replace, and what auth a desktop app can use (session cookie via browser OAuth vs any token mechanism). Server-side gaps are reported as proposed follow-ups, not built unasked.
- Implementation target: the native app line (PR #4 base + perf branch emise/perf-sparse-load, which the worker bases on), because it builds/tests here; design documented so the WinForms app can adopt the same protocol. Conflict rule: if the server scroll changed since fetch, surface it — never silently overwrite.
- Verification: run a local phext-edit instance with a scratch library and exercise sync both directions with byte-identity checks.
- AUTH REFINEMENT (Will, 2026-11-08 00:59 CST): 'Use OAuth support - allow Phext Notepad to authenticate through the SSO providers on edit.phext.io.' OAuth through edit's providers (GitHub/Google) is the directed primary path, not a pasted cookie. Preferred shape against the stock server: embedded-webview OAuth — edit sets its phext_session cookie (host-only, HMAC-sealed, 14-day) in the webview jar; the app extracts and stores it in protected storage and presents it on sync calls; signed-in-but-unapproved must surface edit's refusal faithfully. safe_next (same-site only) from the Mutable SSO work is the constraint to check for any loopback flow. Server-side additions (desktop-aud assertion, loopback allowance) are report-only proposals.

Results:
- LANDED (worker report ~/workspace/phext-notepad-perf/REPORT-SYNC.md; Emise verified remote branch emise/edit-sync @ a9f604e7c4ded048631e6f5d5517bf1722731e90 via API; based on emise/perf-sparse-load 8a3af359; nothing merged, no PR): SERVER SURFACE (fresh lattice exo eb450bc): phext-edit holds exactly ONE open phext process-wide; client routes /api/phexts, /api/open, /api/status, /api/tree, /api/scroll/{coord}, /api/update (memory-only), /api/save, /api/session; NO per-scroll version/etag anywhere — change detection is client-side SHA-256 base hashes (SyncBook per server+phext); auth = phext_session cookie + x-csrf-token on POSTs; editor-list refusal and CSRF refusal surface verbatim in the app. SYNC: scroll granularity only; pull/push classify per scroll; both-moved = conflict, local kept, remote shown, never overwritten; deletions push as cleared scrolls (verified end-to-end); sync refuses to switch the server's one open phext while it holds unsaved edits; editing fully offline, sync explicit-only; Sync menu (Connect/Pull/Pull Current Scroll/Push/Disconnect) + conflict dialog. E2E vs the real phext-edit binary: 36/36 checks + 29/29 core tests, 0 build warnings. DEVIATION from Will's OAuth direction (reported honestly): loopback capture is impossible against the stock server (safe_next clamps next to same-site paths, oauth.rs:1516) and the embedded webview was rejected (FLTK has no webview widget; PR #4's founding design is 'no web view'). AS BUILT: app launches edit's real OAuth start URL (/api/auth/github|google|x) in the system browser — genuine provider sign-in — then the user pastes the phext_session value ONCE per 14 days; app verifies via /api/session, shows identity, stores cookie+CSRF in an owner-only 0600 file. Provider exchange leg untested locally (needs a real GitHub app + human login); everything downstream ran against unmodified server code with harness-minted cookies, including the non-editor refusal verbatim. PROPOSED (not built): POST /api/auth/desktop SSO-assertion exchange (the /api/auth/sso/{aud} machinery already exists) or a device-code flow — either removes the paste. Will must configure NOTHING server-side on real edit.phext.io; standing requirements only (account on editors list, providers configured). NOTE: current lattice source still carries a --token bearer check in Gate::admit — sync neither uses nor depends on it; its removal is Track C (29.7.7/8.6.11/6.5.8).
