# Incorporate AeneasVerif/aeneas and h5i-dev/h5i into research.phext

Coordinate: 41.5.5/6.5.8/5.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-06 23:14 CST
Request (verbatim): incorporate https://github.com/AeneasVerif/aeneas / incorporate https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i
Status: complete — S002 (Aeneas) + S003 (h5i) distilled into research.phext 2026-11-06

Notes:
- Treatment follows the S001 pattern Will ratified: study each repo on its contents (never its cover), then distill into research.phext as source studies with canonical concepts, foundations, Singular compliance, per-iteration commits.
- Findings: Aeneas = Rust→LLBC→pure functional translation to Lean/Coq/F*/HOL4; backward functions for returned mutable borrows; design paper-proved (ICFP 2022/2024), OCaml implementation (77,012 lines) + Charon + hand models trusted; Lean backend dominant (49,782 lines); named deployment SymCrypt ML-KEM. h5i (Takahashi) = NOT small: 26 crates, 150,666 lines Rust + 47,083 Lean, v0.5.4 — verifiable web framework (kernel extracted to Lean VIA AENEAS), receipt-before-bytes red-team proxy, fail-closed agent boxes; the two repos are already connected (h5i drives Aeneas). Distillation: Ch.8 (S002, concepts 1.2.48–1.2.52, cluster G) + Ch.9 (S003, concepts 1.2.53–1.2.56, cluster H); foundations 1.3.81–1.3.83; coinage tenant (1.3.84, pure); narrative v7; Oracle unmoved ~25%; Q18 (Aeneas road vs hand-built model pricing) + Q19 (receipt-before-act for Exocortex agents) added. research.phext: 191 scrolls, sha256 d8033031…, audit residual 0. Studies: ~/workspace/aeneas-study/STUDY.md, ~/workspace/h5i-repo-study/STUDY.md. 56 canonical concepts — restructure trigger at 60 is 4 away.
# Script the proof-tool install in libphext-rs + wire into exocortical setup.sh

Coordinate: 41.8.7/10.9.12/8.8.12
Issued: 2026-11-07 01:17 CST
Request (verbatim): please add a script to libphext-rs so that we can get those tools installed; also incorporate them into setup.sh in exocortical
Status: complete 2026-11-07 — script committed on provable-0.4.1, Phase 11 live in exocortical

Notes:
- Parent task 47.11.7/12.13.16/12.11.16. Recipe lessons to encode: opam install ./src (the ./ is load-bearing; bare 'src' silently no-ops), charon-ml deps via opam install ./charon, aeneas make SERIALLY (parallel MAKEFLAGS races dune's _build lock), charon built with RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN from its rust-toolchain file (nightly-2026-09-17, host target only), Lean version read from aeneas/backends/lean/lean-toolchain (v4.35.0), set -euo pipefail throughout.
- Closed 2026-11-07. scripts/install-proof-tools.sh committed on provable-0.4.1 (cd18d83; published to the remote branch in the PR #7 stack, mode 100755 verified) and exocortical setup.sh gained Phase 11 running it from its /source/libphext-rs clone (published to wbic16/exocortical exo as 34452c9c). The script codifies the recipe verified manually on aletheia-core; not yet run end-to-end from a clean machine.
# phcc phext capability parity with libphext-rs (C developer library)

Coordinate: 41.10.7/11.11.14/11.10.15
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): make sure phcc has every capability libphext-rs has, so developers can quickly handle phext data
Status: COMPLETE + PUSHED @ 8b56ea22 (77/77 parity; 163,831 checks 0 failures under gcc and phcc; fuzz 40,000 cases 0 divergences). D-2 marked RESOLVED in phext/PARITY.md by commit 7ead6f12 (main=exo) after libphext-rs PR #8 merged (in-tree 0.4.2, unpublished).

Notes:
- Phase A parity matrix: ~/workspace/phcc-libphext/PARITY.md (also committed as phext/PARITY.md). 77 capabilities audited from libphext-rs v0.4.1 source: 26 constants, 7 types, 17 Coordinate-surface items, 27 free functions - 77 with C counterparts, 0 gaps.
- Divergences of record: D-2 strict parse returns PHEXT_EFORMAT/PHEXT_ENUMBER where Rust TryFrom panics; D-3 C API byte-oriented, no UTF-8 validation; D-4 map sorted (implode identical); D-5 summary display truncation; D-6 lenient parse wraps like Rust release.
- Phase B: new top-level phext/ dir in a copy of the phcc tree on base 395f5d63 (F1) - phext.h (380 lines), phext.c (1,921 lines, incl. scalar XXH3-128 port), README, tests. Additive only; tcc.h/tccpp.c preprocessor counters untouched - wiring them to the library is the named F3-candidate follow-on, not done.
- Phase C: ported libphext-rs tests (49 test_lib + 8 test_phokenize + 1 regressions = 58 functions, same vectors): 163,831 checks, 0 failures under gcc AND under the freshly built phcc itself on aletheia-core (dogfood; phcc make test also passes). Differential fuzz vs Rust reference driver on libphext-rs 0.4.1: 40,000 cases, 2 seeds, 24 op classes, 0 divergences on defined behaviour (339 Rust panics total, all the D-2 parse class). Fuzz harness kept outside the repo at ~/workspace/phcc-libphext/fuzz/.
