Coordinate: 44.13.9/15.15.18/13.13.19
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): normalize the coordinate space to 1-digit components for both metrics
Status: closed — normalized space published 2026-11-07 (3-digit shipped per escalation rule); honest geometry cost recorded

Notes:
- Follows 28.7.9/10.6.13/6.6.9 (two indexing methods documented). Will directed 2026-11-07 12:30 CST: normalize ultra.phext coordinate space to 1-digit components (1-9 per component) for both metrics.

Results:
- Collision pressure measured per Will amendment: 1-digit 82.77% collisions, 2-digit 51.60%, 3-digit ~45.8% (structural hot-prefix floor) — shipped 3-digit (components 1..999) uniformly for both metrics.
- Design M: components 1-8 identity; component 9 population-quantile re-draw. 146,761 mapped collisions; 150,942 words bumped (47.06%) in build pass order.
- Zero words lost; tiers and per-rule counts identical; verify5.py VERIFY OK, all components in 1..999.
- Neighbourhood cost (corrected figures from the completed measurement, normalize_neighbours.json): panel Spearman mean 0.291 / median 0.404; Jaccard@50 mean 0.184. Per rule: P3/P4 preserve distance ordering best (~0.52); P6 rank keeps neighbour membership best (J@50 0.426) but low ordering (0.249); P1 home ~0.025 (its panel ordering was its shelf-slot axis). Cause: in the log-scaled metric component 9 had the widest range, so panel order was disproportionately a component-9 ordering; compressing it reweights the geometry. Docs (BUILD-REPORT.md, indexing-methods doc, normalize_stats.json) corrected to the true figures.
- Published: 58,166,306 B, SHA-256 caf74ebf53f72f6d0ef9972ccd2277ce720fcf3c603c099f8b3317267a2606f5, wbic16/human@exo commit 894bffb1; remote blob verified by API + fresh-clone re-hash; published phext intro unaffected (states only exact bump counts).
# Desktop SSO-assertion endpoint for Phext Notepad (remove the cookie-paste step)

Coordinate: 46.5.5/6.5.10/5.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-08 01:21 CST
Request (verbatim): Build the desktop SSO-assertion endpoint next
Status: done — built, verified end to end, both branches pushed 2026-11-08; merge + deploy + arming are Will’s acts

Notes:
- Follows Track B (39.4.7/7.4.9/5.5.9): the notepad's edit.phext.io sign-in works through OAuth but requires pasting the phext_session value once per 14 days, because safe_next clamps returns to same-site paths and no webview exists in the FLTK app. Will approved building the server-side fix.
- Design spine (from the Mutable SSO machinery, task 27.6.8/7.5.9/6.5.8 + generalization 13.6.8/7.6.9/6.6.9): reuse the 120-second single-use signed assertion under PHEXT_SSO_SECRET with a new 'desktop' audience. KEY SECURITY CONSTRAINT: a shipped desktop binary cannot hold the shared HMAC secret, so verification must happen SERVER-side — the app receives the assertion at a loopback return and exchanges it at a new server endpoint, which verifies + burns the jti server-side and returns a session credential the app stores and presents. Loopback-only return validation for this audience; assertion stays 120s/single-use.
- Branch strategy to determine from live state: the generalized /api/auth/sso/<aud> allowlist (mutable, exocortexia, wishnode) lives on unmerged branch emise/sso-exocortexia @ 122ff68; compose with it rather than forking a parallel shape. Track C's token/footer branch (ca6495ce) does not touch the SSO endpoints (per its report) — minimal conflict surface, noted for Will's merge order.
- Notepad half: automated Connect flow on the emise/edit-sync line (loopback listener -> browser OAuth -> assertion -> exchange -> stored session), paste kept as fallback when the server lacks the desktop audience (404). Merge/deploy of lattice changes remain Will's acts, plus whatever arming env the design needs.
- DONE 2026-11-08. Lattice branch emise/sso-desktop @ 65cb909d (base: exo eb450bc — the brief’s base emise/sso-exocortexia @ 122ff68 had been MERGED into exo via PR #26, verified ancestor, so the branch sits on exo directly). Notepad branch emise/desktop-sso @ c83778ed (base emise/edit-sync @ a9f604e7, exact). Server: PHEXT_SSO_DESKTOP=1 arms the desktop audience (flag, not a URL — the return is a per-attempt loopback listener); loopback_return admits only http://127.0.0.1 or [::1] literals with an explicit port (localhost/https/names rejected, tested); the attempt state nonce rides sealed as the assertion’s optional st claim (web assertions byte-shape unchanged); POST /api/auth/desktop/exchange verifies under PHEXT_SSO_SECRET, burns the jti server-side, checks the editors list fresh, and returns a freshly sealed session + CSRF as JSON (Oauth::issue_session factored out of the OAuth finish). Non-editor: 403 with the gate’s exact refusal, no credential, assertion still spent. Tests: lattice 176 (166 + 10 new), notepad core 33 (29 + 4), app builds. Joint E2E vs the real phext-edit binary + real sync_probe: 27/27 legs (full desktop-login flow, exchanged-session pull/edit/push round trip persisted to disk, replay/tamper/wrong-state/localhost/https/unknown-aud negatives, unarmed 404s + probe fallback signal, non-editor 403). Provider credential leg remains human-only (harness session cookie stands in), same honest limit as Track B. Report: ~/workspace/phext-notepad-perf/REPORT-DESKTOP-SSO.md. Remaining (Will): merge order in the report’s runbook; deploy; add PHEXT_SSO_DESKTOP=1 to /etc/phext-edit/oauth.env; restart phext-edit.
- Report inscribed in artifacts.phext at 33.6.9/8.6.11/7.5.9 (report sha256 be4f829a…); artifacts.phext pushed to wbic16/human@exo commit 90dd1ff98fd6, remote blob sha256 fc04b9f2eb17… verified byte-identical to local.
